WEBVTT

00:41.341 --> 00:44.679
(electricity buzzing)

00:53.621 --> 00:55.924
[Student] Well, well,
if it isn't Yuta Okkotsu,

00:56.056 --> 00:57.859
my favorite weakling.

00:57.992 --> 01:00.060
[Yuta] Don't you come near me.

01:00.193 --> 01:03.196
Oh, come on, don't
play hard to get.

01:04.766 --> 01:06.400
[Yuta] I said don't.

01:06.534 --> 01:10.572
I just wanna slug you one
more time before I graduate.

01:10.705 --> 01:12.040
(student giggles)

01:12.172 --> 01:15.309
You're not gonna deny me my
graduation present, are you?

01:15.442 --> 01:18.445
Since it's our
last time together.

01:18.580 --> 01:20.882
Maybe I should just kill you.

01:21.015 --> 01:22.082
Don't touch me.

01:22.215 --> 01:23.150
Rika.

01:23.283 --> 01:24.752
(student grunts)

01:24.886 --> 01:25.920
What you say?

01:26.054 --> 01:28.856
(student grunts)

01:30.925 --> 01:33.828
(rain splattering)

01:35.029 --> 01:36.229
I'm sorry.

01:36.864 --> 01:37.865
I'm sorry.

01:39.634 --> 01:40.635
I'm sorry.

01:41.368 --> 01:42.369
I'm sorry.

01:42.570 --> 01:44.672
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

01:45.607 --> 01:46.674
I'm sorry.

01:46.808 --> 01:47.809
I'm sorry.

01:49.978 --> 01:52.814
(door creaking)

02:06.594 --> 02:09.797
[Satoru] A complete cover-up
and a secret execution?

02:09.931 --> 02:11.599
Boy, that's some story.

02:12.767 --> 02:15.770
[Director] The child in
question did consent, though.

02:15.903 --> 02:17.105
He's underage.

02:17.237 --> 02:18.973
Just 16-years-old.

02:19.107 --> 02:22.610
And who knows how many he's
cursed to death so far.

02:22.744 --> 02:24.378
He's already turned the tables

02:24.512 --> 02:28.549
on three grade-two sorcerers
and a grade-one sorcerer.

02:29.684 --> 02:32.620
Which is exactly the
reason you've turned to me,

02:34.421 --> 02:36.658
or have you forgotten that?

02:36.791 --> 02:37.525
(director grunts)

02:37.659 --> 02:39.192
[Director] So, you'll take him?

02:39.326 --> 02:40.695
Yes.

02:40.828 --> 02:44.866
Yuta Okkotsu, will
attend Jujutsu High School.

02:48.670 --> 02:52.305
You make this in shop
class, Yuta Okkotsu?

02:54.008 --> 02:56.243
[Yuta] It used to be a knife.

02:58.012 --> 03:03.417
I tried killing myself
but Rika wouldn't let me.

03:05.987 --> 03:06.888
Kinda dark.

03:08.188 --> 03:09.857
(metal clanging)

03:09.991 --> 03:11.224
Guess what?

03:11.358 --> 03:13.161
You're starting at
a new school today.

03:13.293 --> 03:14.696
I'm not going.

03:14.829 --> 03:15.830
Hmm.

03:17.932 --> 03:21.169
[Yuta] I don't want to
hurt anyone anymore,

03:21.301 --> 03:23.236
so I'm never going
outside again.

03:24.872 --> 03:26.507
Never?

03:26.641 --> 03:28.910
You're gonna get
pretty lonely that way.

03:31.813 --> 03:33.715
The curse that was
placed upon you.

03:33.848 --> 03:36.416
It's a curse that
can save people, too,

03:36.551 --> 03:38.886
depending on how
it's used, of course.

03:40.154 --> 03:43.524
My advice to you is learn
how to use that power.

03:43.658 --> 03:46.961
You can cast it all away
later if you still decide to.

03:52.499 --> 03:55.435
(leaves rustling)

04:01.008 --> 04:03.945
(gentle music)

04:04.078 --> 04:06.848
(woman vocalizing)

04:44.752 --> 04:49.924
♪ You don't see at all ♪

04:50.591 --> 04:55.062
♪ What's right for you to do ♪

04:55.797 --> 04:59.432
♪ But let's start it now ♪

04:59.567 --> 05:04.038
♪ Take a deep breath ♪

05:04.172 --> 05:09.376
♪ You're moving forward ♪

05:10.812 --> 05:13.614
♪ Deciding not to look back ♪

05:13.748 --> 05:18.953
♪ Your weakness is your
greatest strength ♪

05:22.322 --> 05:24.625
♪ To make it to the end ♪

05:24.759 --> 05:29.697
♪ You'll feel won't be alone ♪

05:55.957 --> 06:00.962
♪ You alone is the
right place to be ♪

06:02.462 --> 06:05.498
♪ Don't be afraid to fall ♪

06:08.102 --> 06:11.072
(man singing faintly)

06:12.273 --> 06:17.444
♪ You will feel that
you can do anything ♪

06:18.312 --> 06:21.682
(man singing faintly)

06:39.567 --> 06:42.402
(birds chirping)

06:42.536 --> 06:45.773
Did you hear about the new
transfer student coming today?

06:45.907 --> 06:49.076
They say he stuffed four of
his old classmates in a locker.

06:49.210 --> 06:50.278
You mean he killed them?

06:50.410 --> 06:52.013
[Toge] Tuna mayo?

06:52.146 --> 06:53.948
No, gravely injured.

06:54.081 --> 06:55.216
(Maki sighs)

06:55.349 --> 06:58.219
Well, if he's cocky, I'll
put him in his place.

06:58.352 --> 07:00.121
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

07:00.254 --> 07:01.122
(air whooshes)

07:01.255 --> 07:02.556
Students of all grades,

07:02.690 --> 07:05.960
we have a new student.

07:06.093 --> 07:08.129
Give him a hand.

07:10.731 --> 07:11.966
Not one hand.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.903
I heard that the kid's
a real wet blanket.

07:16.037 --> 07:19.974
The last thing I need is another
moody rookie to look after.

07:20.107 --> 07:21.108
[Toge] Salmon.

07:21.242 --> 07:22.109
Hmm.

07:23.611 --> 07:25.146
(Satoru sighs)

07:25.279 --> 07:26.479
Oh, well, then.

07:27.748 --> 07:29.784
You can come on in now.

07:29.917 --> 07:32.753
[Yuta] I sense a really
dark mood in there.

07:39.459 --> 07:41.162
[Maki] I'll just ignore him.

07:44.131 --> 07:46.968
(ground rumbling)

07:50.604 --> 07:53.808
(suspenseful music)

07:54.408 --> 07:56.043
Huh?

07:56.177 --> 07:58.112
(upbeat music)

07:58.245 --> 07:59.347
I'm Yuta.

07:59.479 --> 08:00.848
- (sword whooshes)
- (metal clangs)

08:00.982 --> 08:03.284
Is this some kind of test?

08:03.417 --> 08:05.186
(Yuta sighs)

08:05.319 --> 08:06.520
Hey.

08:07.688 --> 08:10.791
Don't you know that
you are cursed?

08:10.925 --> 08:13.361
This is a place to
learn about curses.

08:13.493 --> 08:16.130
Not a place for the cursed
to be hanging around.

08:19.066 --> 08:21.369
The number of people that
die mysterious deaths

08:21.502 --> 08:25.973
or go missing in Japan is
over 10,000 a year on average.

08:26.107 --> 08:29.377
The majority of those are
actually not accidents,

08:29.510 --> 08:30.845
but caused by curses.

08:30.978 --> 08:32.546
Born from negative emotions.

08:32.680 --> 08:36.283
Among them are also some evil
cases caused by curse users.

08:36.417 --> 08:40.154
You see, only curses
can affect other curses.

08:40.287 --> 08:41.789
(Yuta gasps)

08:41.922 --> 08:44.558
This place is where we learn
curses to exorcize curses.

08:44.692 --> 08:47.228
Welcome to Tokyo
Jujutsu High School.

08:49.530 --> 08:52.033
[Yuta] He's just
telling me this now?

08:52.166 --> 08:53.167
[All] What?

08:53.834 --> 08:56.505
He's just telling him that now?

08:56.637 --> 08:57.838
My bad.

08:58.806 --> 09:01.242
Oh, you all should back
away pretty quickly.

09:01.375 --> 09:02.243
[All] Huh?

09:04.345 --> 09:06.914
(Panda groans)

09:07.848 --> 09:09.183
[Rika] Do not.

09:10.217 --> 09:11.352
Stop it.

09:11.485 --> 09:13.054
Rika.

09:13.187 --> 09:14.855
[Rika] Bully Yuta.

09:22.696 --> 09:26.000
(birds chirping)

09:26.133 --> 09:26.901
(kid giggles)

09:27.034 --> 09:28.169
[Girl] Over there, over there.

09:28.302 --> 09:29.203
- (kid giggles)
- [Boy] What is it?

09:29.336 --> 09:30.337
What is it?

09:31.138 --> 09:34.141
Yuta, I have a
birthday gift for you.

09:34.275 --> 09:35.576
(Yuta groans)

09:35.709 --> 09:37.111
Hmm.

09:37.244 --> 09:38.212
(Yuta chuckles)

09:38.345 --> 09:40.014
Thank you.

09:40.147 --> 09:41.082
Can I open it?

09:41.215 --> 09:42.083
[Rika] Go ahead.

09:42.216 --> 09:43.084
(Yuta chuckles)

09:43.217 --> 09:43.951
Really?

09:44.085 --> 09:46.787
[Rika] Yes, I said go ahead.

09:51.092 --> 09:51.759
Huh?

09:51.892 --> 09:53.060
It's a ring.

09:53.694 --> 09:55.729
[Rika] An engagement ring.

09:55.863 --> 09:57.298
[Yuta] Engagement?

09:57.431 --> 10:00.201
(romantic music)

10:09.076 --> 10:12.246
It's a promise that
when we grow up,

10:13.180 --> 10:15.282
we're going to get
married to each other.

10:17.451 --> 10:20.654
(car crashes)

10:20.788 --> 10:21.822
(woman shouts)

10:21.956 --> 10:23.090
[Driver] I didn't
mean to hit her.

10:23.224 --> 10:24.792
[Man] Someone,
call an ambulance.

10:24.925 --> 10:26.293
[Woman] Look at her,
call the coroner.

10:26.427 --> 10:28.662
(woman sighs) There's no
way she's gonna make it.

10:28.796 --> 10:29.763
[Man] What happened?

10:29.897 --> 10:31.499
[Woman] Her head's crushed in.

10:31.632 --> 10:32.900
[Man] How horrible.

10:33.033 --> 10:34.768
[Man] Yes, a child
got run over by a car.

10:34.902 --> 10:36.538
I don't know, hurry.

10:36.670 --> 10:38.038
[Man] We should help her.

10:38.172 --> 10:39.508
[Woman] I'm not going near that.

10:39.640 --> 10:40.774
[Man] That poor girl.

10:40.908 --> 10:42.176
[Woman] Oh, this
is heartbreaking.

10:42.309 --> 10:43.310
Rika?

10:45.279 --> 10:46.380
[Rika] Yuta.

10:48.315 --> 10:50.317
(Yuta groans)

10:50.451 --> 10:53.254
(suspenseful music)

10:55.823 --> 10:57.024
Yuta.

10:59.927 --> 11:02.363
When we grow up,

11:02.663 --> 11:06.967
we're gonna get married.

11:07.268 --> 11:11.372
- (suspenseful music)
- (Yuta groans)

11:11.506 --> 11:12.740
It's a promise.

11:12.873 --> 11:14.141
So, as you can see,

11:14.275 --> 11:15.976
this boy was cursed
by his friend Rika,

11:16.110 --> 11:18.279
who is still madly
in love with him.

11:18.412 --> 11:23.817
Be nice to him or else
Rika will get you.

11:24.451 --> 11:25.486
(Panda groans)

11:25.620 --> 11:27.054
Remember, if you attack Yuta,

11:27.188 --> 11:30.224
Rika's curse will activate
or maybe it won't.

11:30.357 --> 11:31.425
It's hard to say.

11:31.560 --> 11:34.228
So be careful, everyone.

11:34.361 --> 11:35.829
Now he tells us.

11:35.963 --> 11:38.299
Since these students
are acting all cool.

11:38.432 --> 11:40.635
Let me introduce them
to you real quick-like.

11:40.768 --> 11:43.204
[Yuta] I have a feeling
this teacher's the problem,

11:43.337 --> 11:44.606
not the students.

11:44.738 --> 11:47.208
[Satoru] This is the cursed
tool user, Maki Zen'in.

11:47.341 --> 11:50.177
She uses special tools
to exorcize curses.

11:51.345 --> 11:53.847
This is the cursed speech
user, Toge Inumaki.

11:53.981 --> 11:55.783
He can only speak in
rice ball ingredients,

11:55.916 --> 11:57.318
so have fun chatting.

11:57.451 --> 11:58.319
[Toge] Kelp.

11:58.452 --> 11:59.320
[Satoru] And Panda.

11:59.453 --> 12:00.387
Hi, I'm Panda.

12:00.522 --> 12:02.056
It's nice to meet you.

12:02.189 --> 12:05.025
Okay, you're all set.

12:05.159 --> 12:08.229
[Yuta] But I'm still not
sure what I'm doing here.

12:08.362 --> 12:09.531
All right then,

12:09.664 --> 12:12.800
our first year class is
a solid four students.

12:12.933 --> 12:15.704
[Yuta] Three students
and one animal anyway.

12:15.836 --> 12:18.205
For your afternoon
jujutsu practice,

12:18.339 --> 12:20.474
you'll be in pairs
of two on two.

12:20.609 --> 12:22.644
Toge and Panda, you're one pair.

12:22.776 --> 12:24.144
All right.

12:24.278 --> 12:26.413
[Satoru] And Maki,
you're with Yuta.

12:26.548 --> 12:27.748
DOE.

12:27.881 --> 12:29.817
Did she just say DOE?

12:29.950 --> 12:32.920
(birds chirping)

12:35.489 --> 12:39.527
Hey, I really hope
we can work together.

12:41.929 --> 12:44.999
You were bullied,
I can totally tell.

12:45.132 --> 12:47.268
(lightning crashes)

12:47.401 --> 12:49.236
(Yuta groans)

12:49.370 --> 12:51.772
I take it by that lame
reaction, I'm right.

12:51.905 --> 12:54.475
I totally get it,
I'd bully you too.

12:54.609 --> 12:55.744
(Yuta groans)

12:55.876 --> 12:57.344
Maybe it's because
you're cursed?

12:57.478 --> 12:59.581
It's written on your face
that you're trying to come off

12:59.714 --> 13:00.582
as a goody-two-shoes.

13:00.715 --> 13:01.750
It's sickening.

13:01.882 --> 13:03.050
(Yuta gasps)

13:03.183 --> 13:04.318
Why are you acting
like the victim

13:04.451 --> 13:06.253
when you're the one
being protected?

13:06.387 --> 13:08.856
I bet, you've been
passive your whole life.

13:08.989 --> 13:10.291
(Yuta groans)

13:10.424 --> 13:12.727
Believe me, Jujutsu High
isn't gonna be that easy.

13:13.427 --> 13:15.963
You're gonna have to step
up if you wanna make it.

13:16.096 --> 13:17.498
(Yuta groans)

13:17.632 --> 13:18.533
Maki.

13:18.667 --> 13:20.467
That's enough of that.

13:20.602 --> 13:21.569
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

13:22.570 --> 13:24.305
Okay, fine.

13:24.438 --> 13:25.540
Get off my case.

13:26.608 --> 13:28.042
Sorry about her.

13:28.175 --> 13:29.810
She has a bad habit of
thinking she's an authority

13:29.943 --> 13:31.145
on mind-reading.

13:31.845 --> 13:34.582
No, she's right.

13:40.087 --> 13:41.455
(footsteps tapping)

13:41.589 --> 13:42.856
Where are we?

13:42.990 --> 13:44.526
[Satoru] It's just
an elementary school.

13:44.659 --> 13:45.859
[Yuta] Huh?

13:45.993 --> 13:47.828
Or rather, just an
elementary school

13:47.961 --> 13:49.830
where some children
have gone missing.

13:49.963 --> 13:51.332
Gone missing?

13:51.465 --> 13:53.601
[Satoru] It happens a
lot in places like this.

13:53.735 --> 13:57.071
It's probably the work of a
naturally-occurring curse.

13:57.971 --> 13:59.440
(Yuta gulps)

13:59.574 --> 14:01.643
Are you saying a curse
actually kidnapped some kids?

14:01.776 --> 14:04.445
Yup, two kids so far.

14:04.579 --> 14:07.448
Curses tend to settle
in spots like these.

14:07.582 --> 14:10.317
Places where bad
memories occurred.

14:11.586 --> 14:13.688
Schools, hospitals.

14:13.822 --> 14:15.189
Places often remembered

14:15.322 --> 14:18.660
with negative emotions are
a receptacle for curses.

14:18.793 --> 14:20.094
As those emotions build up,

14:20.227 --> 14:22.463
they can cause a
curse to be born.

14:22.597 --> 14:23.598
Like it was here.

14:24.699 --> 14:27.000
We're here to exorcize the
curse, and save the kids

14:27.134 --> 14:29.002
Or retrieve them
if they're dead.

14:29.136 --> 14:30.538
(Yuta groans)

14:30.672 --> 14:31.539
Dead?

14:33.374 --> 14:36.210
Emerge from darkness
blacker still.

14:36.343 --> 14:38.847
Purify that which is impure.

14:38.979 --> 14:42.383
(veil crackling)

14:42.517 --> 14:43.484
Huh?

14:43.618 --> 14:45.653
It's turning into night.

14:46.987 --> 14:48.389
It's a veil.

14:48.523 --> 14:51.191
A barrier of sorts to
help smoke out the curses.

14:51.325 --> 14:53.595
It also keeps us hidden
from the outside.

14:55.329 --> 14:58.031
It's pretty easy to
undo from inside.

15:00.702 --> 15:02.403
Do be careful now, you two.

15:03.571 --> 15:04.572
Try not to die.

15:05.640 --> 15:07.542
Die? Gojo?

15:07.675 --> 15:08.543
[Maki] Transfer student.

15:08.676 --> 15:09.677
Huh?

15:10.477 --> 15:12.547
Don't let yourself
get distracted.

15:12.680 --> 15:15.683
(suspenseful music)

15:17.752 --> 15:18.620
Put

15:19.420 --> 15:20.421
me

15:21.088 --> 15:22.289
On!

15:23.023 --> 15:25.527
(Yuta groans)

15:26.728 --> 15:27.595
Put me on.

15:29.930 --> 15:31.833
[Yuta] They're coming this way.

15:31.965 --> 15:32.901
What do we do?

15:33.033 --> 15:34.602
Stop screaming.

15:34.736 --> 15:37.004
(air whooshing)

15:37.137 --> 15:38.439
(suspenseful music)

15:38.573 --> 15:41.810
Just remember this,
the weaker curses are,

15:41.942 --> 15:43.578
the more they group together.

15:44.579 --> 15:47.414
(stick whooshing)

15:49.383 --> 15:52.986
Of course, the same could
be said for human beings.

15:53.120 --> 15:54.421
[Yuta] Incredible.

15:54.556 --> 15:56.591
She wiped them all out
with a single blow.

15:58.392 --> 16:00.093
Okay, let's get a move on.

16:00.227 --> 16:01.295
[Yuta] Huh?

16:01.428 --> 16:02.630
Where to?

16:02.764 --> 16:04.566
Inside, obviously.

16:07.100 --> 16:10.538
(Yuta breathes deeply)

16:14.742 --> 16:16.310
Miss Zen'in, aren't you

16:16.443 --> 16:18.613
at least a little bit
scared of this place?

16:18.746 --> 16:20.314
Don't use my last name.

16:21.148 --> 16:22.550
Sorry.

16:22.684 --> 16:25.219
It's just, this place is
really giving me the creeps.

16:25.352 --> 16:28.388
It's exactly the type of
place where ghosts would be.

16:28.523 --> 16:29.958
[Maki] There aren't
many curses here,

16:30.090 --> 16:31.992
even though the
veil's been drawn.

16:33.126 --> 16:35.663
No, they are here,

16:35.797 --> 16:37.464
they're just not attacking.

16:38.432 --> 16:41.301
I wonder, is it
because he's here?

16:41.636 --> 16:42.302
(Yuta groans)

16:42.436 --> 16:43.671
Something just moved.

16:43.805 --> 16:44.706
[Maki] Hey?

16:44.839 --> 16:45.807
[Yuta] What?

16:45.940 --> 16:47.542
[Maki] What grade are you?

16:48.475 --> 16:50.043
[Yuta] Like in school?

16:50.177 --> 16:53.615
Jujutsu sorcerers are ranked
in grades from four to one.

16:53.748 --> 16:55.148
Yeah, but, I only started

16:55.282 --> 16:57.752
at Jujutsu High
School this week.

16:57.886 --> 16:59.654
I don't think I'm ranked yet.

16:59.787 --> 17:00.655
(Maki grunts)

17:00.788 --> 17:02.155
Forget it.

17:02.289 --> 17:03.691
Show me your student ID.

17:03.825 --> 17:06.594
The one you got from that
dumb blindfolded guy.

17:07.461 --> 17:09.062
Dumb blindfolded guy?

17:10.698 --> 17:12.366
Okay, here you go.

17:12.499 --> 17:16.638
Well, if you just joined,
you're probably a grade four.

17:16.771 --> 17:17.705
Special-grade?

17:18.940 --> 17:22.409
Special-grade is even a
higher ranking than Grade One,

17:22.544 --> 17:25.947
This must be some kind of a
practical joke or something.

17:26.079 --> 17:26.948
Miss Zen'in.

17:27.080 --> 17:27.949
Miss Zen'in.

17:28.081 --> 17:29.249
Behind you.

17:29.851 --> 17:32.252
(monster crackling)

17:32.386 --> 17:35.055
- (ground rumbles)
- (Yuta groans)

17:35.188 --> 17:37.725
(explosion booms)

17:37.859 --> 17:40.862
(monster growls)

17:40.995 --> 17:41.896
(monster growls)

17:42.030 --> 17:43.631
(Yuta screams)

17:43.765 --> 17:45.198
[Maki] Shit.

17:45.332 --> 17:46.768
You're way too damn big.

17:48.036 --> 17:49.971
(Maki shouts)

17:50.103 --> 17:52.306
(monster growls)

17:52.439 --> 17:55.977
- (metal clangs)
- (Maki grunts)

17:56.109 --> 17:57.411
(monster gulps)

17:57.545 --> 17:58.513
Yum.

17:59.047 --> 18:00.682
(monster burps)

18:00.815 --> 18:02.750
Thank you for the meal.

18:05.620 --> 18:06.486
(foot thuds)

18:06.621 --> 18:07.287
Shit.

18:07.421 --> 18:08.890
I dropped my cursed tool.

18:09.023 --> 18:10.792
Let us out of here.

18:14.194 --> 18:15.495
Where are we now?

18:15.630 --> 18:17.799
We're stuck in this
dumb curse's stomach.

18:17.932 --> 18:20.535
No reason to go
passing out over this.

18:20.668 --> 18:22.604
You mean that curse ate us?

18:22.737 --> 18:25.272
That's right. And I thought you
were supposed to be protected

18:25.405 --> 18:26.908
by that curse of yours?

18:27.041 --> 18:28.342
[Yuta] Don't blame me,

18:28.475 --> 18:30.578
I have no idea what makes
Rika decide to come out.

18:30.712 --> 18:32.479
But what are we gonna do now?

18:32.614 --> 18:34.448
After a while the
veil will go away,

18:34.582 --> 18:36.149
and help will come for us.

18:36.283 --> 18:37.150
(Maki grunts)

18:37.284 --> 18:38.452
Embarrassing.

18:38.586 --> 18:39.721
Shit.

18:39.854 --> 18:40.989
[Boy] Please help.

18:41.121 --> 18:41.990
Hmm?

18:42.122 --> 18:42.991
Who's there?

18:43.123 --> 18:44.092
Please help me,

18:44.224 --> 18:45.893
my friend's about to die.

18:47.061 --> 18:48.830
(Yuta groans)

18:48.963 --> 18:50.397
(Yuta gulps)

18:50.531 --> 18:53.101
Are you saying a curse
actually kidnapped some kid?

18:53.233 --> 18:55.435
Yup, two kids so far.

18:55.570 --> 18:58.338
We're here to exorcize the
curse, and save the kids

18:58.472 --> 19:00.307
or retrieve them
if they're dead.

19:00.975 --> 19:02.275
Thank goodness.

19:02.409 --> 19:03.578
They're alive.

19:03.711 --> 19:04.812
Just barely.

19:04.946 --> 19:05.813
Huh?

19:05.947 --> 19:06.814
Look at them closer.

19:07.815 --> 19:11.451
The big one's obviously been
affected by the curse, too.

19:11.586 --> 19:13.721
Both of them could
die at any minute.

19:15.089 --> 19:15.957
Oh, no.

19:16.090 --> 19:16.958
(Yuta groans)

19:17.091 --> 19:17.959
What do we do?

19:18.092 --> 19:19.459
I told you.

19:19.594 --> 19:21.796
All we can do is wait for help.

19:21.929 --> 19:23.463
Not everyone's like you.

19:23.598 --> 19:26.400
Most people don't have
resistance to curses.

19:27.300 --> 19:28.168
Huh?

19:28.301 --> 19:29.469
Miss Zen'in?

19:30.038 --> 19:31.673
(Maki groans)

19:31.806 --> 19:32.807
Maki.

19:35.009 --> 19:35.943
(Yuta gasps)

19:36.077 --> 19:37.812
What kind of wound is this?

19:39.614 --> 19:42.315
Does this mean
you're cursed now?

19:42.449 --> 19:44.886
Is she going to die?

19:47.220 --> 19:49.824
Please, I don't want to die too.

19:50.958 --> 19:52.259
(boy cries)

19:52.392 --> 19:53.594
Please.

19:54.629 --> 19:56.531
I don't know how to save you.

19:57.699 --> 19:58.566
I'm sorry.

19:58.700 --> 19:59.801
Okkotsu.

19:59.934 --> 20:04.072
Tell me, why did you
come to Jujutsu High?

20:04.204 --> 20:05.807
What is it you wanna do?

20:08.009 --> 20:08.876
What do you want?

20:09.010 --> 20:09.944
What're your goals?

20:10.078 --> 20:11.846
What are you trying to achieve?

20:12.814 --> 20:17.151
I just don't wanna see
anyone getting hurt again.

20:18.119 --> 20:21.689
I tried to lock myself
away and disappear.

20:22.690 --> 20:26.027
But Gojo warned me
I'd be too lonely.

20:26.160 --> 20:27.862
And I couldn't argue with him.

20:29.697 --> 20:32.133
I don't want to be all alone.

20:32.265 --> 20:34.936
I want to be needed by someone.

20:35.069 --> 20:38.906
I want it to be all right
to know that I'm alive.

20:41.542 --> 20:42.844
Fine, do it then.

20:44.879 --> 20:47.949
Keep exorcizing curses
over and over again.

20:48.816 --> 20:50.585
And when you get good at it,

20:50.718 --> 20:52.954
confidence and
friends will find you.

20:54.354 --> 20:59.560
That's why we're
here at Jujutsu High.

20:59.927 --> 21:02.029
(gentle music)

21:08.970 --> 21:11.139
(metal clangs)

21:11.271 --> 21:12.472
Rika.

21:13.608 --> 21:14.809
[Rika] Yes, Yuta?

21:16.844 --> 21:19.279
[Yuta] Lend me your strength.

21:19.412 --> 21:21.983
(metal dings)

21:22.116 --> 21:24.919
(monster groans)

21:28.321 --> 21:31.692
(Rika screams)

21:31.826 --> 21:32.827
Who are you?

21:32.960 --> 21:33.961
Who are you?

21:35.096 --> 21:37.598
(Rika grunts)

21:42.804 --> 21:46.007
[Rika] That's enough out of you.

21:48.009 --> 21:48.876
(blood splashes)

21:49.010 --> 21:50.377
Now that's terrifying.

21:51.444 --> 21:53.681
Rika Orimoto at her strongest.

21:53.815 --> 21:55.917
Impressive special-grade curse.

21:57.051 --> 21:58.152
(Satoru giggles)

21:58.286 --> 21:59.520
So scary.

22:00.888 --> 22:01.889
Oh, wow.

22:02.523 --> 22:03.724
Look at me.

22:04.491 --> 22:05.860
I'm so pretty.

22:07.427 --> 22:09.462
I love it.

22:10.998 --> 22:13.701
(Yuta groans)

22:19.173 --> 22:20.373
All right.

22:20.508 --> 22:22.810
It's just a little
further everybody.

22:23.845 --> 22:27.114
I need to get Miss Zen'in
and these kids to Gojo.

22:27.248 --> 22:30.885
Hopefully, Rika keeps
those curses distracted.

22:31.018 --> 22:33.521
(Yuta groans)

22:35.189 --> 22:37.892
(Yuta grunts)

22:40.027 --> 22:41.963
I can't stop.

22:43.396 --> 22:44.999
Not yet.

22:45.132 --> 22:47.835
(Yuta grunts)

22:49.402 --> 22:52.006
I'm not gonna be weak anymore.

22:52.139 --> 22:53.507
I'm gonna change.

22:53.641 --> 22:54.842
Here and now.

22:57.377 --> 23:01.148
[Rika] Yuta, you can do it.

23:06.087 --> 23:07.154
Yes, I can.

23:08.089 --> 23:10.892
(gentle music)

23:12.660 --> 23:13.861
Welcome back.

23:15.162 --> 23:16.163
You did well.

23:23.470 --> 23:26.741
They say both Maki and the
kids are going to be fine.

23:27.708 --> 23:29.043
That's a relief.

23:30.011 --> 23:32.546
Funny, you don't look
very relieved to me.

23:34.248 --> 23:35.650
I did it.

23:35.783 --> 23:38.319
I managed to call
Rika out by myself.

23:38.451 --> 23:39.620
Oh, really?

23:39.754 --> 23:41.856
That's a big step forward.

23:41.989 --> 23:44.225
(wheels creaking)

23:44.358 --> 23:47.061
(Yuta groans)

23:49.263 --> 23:51.999
(gentle music)

23:55.102 --> 23:57.972
(Yuta coughing)

24:26.400 --> 24:28.769
[Yuta] Okay, I'm gonna spin you.

24:28.903 --> 24:31.138
(Rika and Yuta giggles)

24:31.272 --> 24:32.940
Stop, Yuta.

24:33.074 --> 24:36.711
I said stop, you're
gonna make me fall.

24:36.844 --> 24:38.980
(Rika and Yuta giggles)

24:39.113 --> 24:40.448
- [Yuta] Rika, you got me.
- [Rika] There.

24:40.581 --> 24:41.849
- Take that.
- (Rika and Yuta giggles)

24:41.983 --> 24:43.384
[Yuta] You better watch out.

24:43.517 --> 24:47.021
(Rika and Yuta giggles)

24:52.393 --> 24:55.262
[Rika] It's a promise
that when we both grow up,

24:55.396 --> 24:57.865
we're going to get
married to each other.

24:59.166 --> 25:00.368
Okay.

25:00.501 --> 25:03.204
(Rika groans)

25:05.006 --> 25:08.542
We'll be together,
forever and ever.

25:09.443 --> 25:10.644
All the time.

25:13.314 --> 25:14.849
[Satoru] You okay?

25:16.217 --> 25:17.151
Yeah.

25:17.284 --> 25:20.154
I was just
remembering something.

25:21.222 --> 25:24.959
I'm starting to think Rika
didn't curse me after all.

25:25.092 --> 25:28.162
I think I might have been
the one who cursed Rika.

25:30.831 --> 25:32.666
You very well may be right.

25:32.800 --> 25:35.504
There's no curse more
twisted than love.

25:35.636 --> 25:38.272
(Yuta cries)

25:42.843 --> 25:45.880
All right, while
I'm at Jujutsu High,

25:46.013 --> 25:48.883
there's something
I want to learn.

25:49.016 --> 25:51.152
I want to break Rika's curse.

25:57.391 --> 25:58.192
(ambulance siren wailing)

25:58.325 --> 26:01.028
(door creaks)

26:02.263 --> 26:05.266
(footsteps tapping)

26:11.839 --> 26:14.041
[Director] The special-grade
cursed apparition,

26:14.175 --> 26:18.979
Rika Orimoto was fully
manifested for 442 seconds.

26:19.346 --> 26:22.049
We entrusted you with
Yuta Okkotsu precisely

26:22.183 --> 26:24.985
so we could prevent
this sort of thing.

26:25.119 --> 26:27.321
There's no room
for excuses, Gojo.

26:27.455 --> 26:30.791
Well, that's good, because
I don't have any excuses.

26:30.925 --> 26:32.927
[Director] How can
you joke about this?

26:33.060 --> 26:35.830
If Rika Orimoto had
remained out of control,

26:35.963 --> 26:38.365
she could have wiped
out an entire town.

26:38.499 --> 26:41.635
If she had I would have
risked my life to stop her.

26:41.769 --> 26:43.737
Listen, now that we've seen it,

26:43.871 --> 26:46.740
there's only one thing we
can say about that curse.

26:46.874 --> 26:49.343
And that's I don't understand.

26:49.477 --> 26:50.778
Why did a little girl

26:50.911 --> 26:53.214
who wasn't from any line
of jujutsu sorcerers,

26:53.347 --> 26:56.050
become such an immense
and powerful curse?

26:56.183 --> 27:00.020
We can't control something
that we don't understand.

27:01.021 --> 27:02.957
So, it's just gonna
take trial and error.

27:03.090 --> 27:06.026
Leave it alone for a while,
and see how it works out.

27:06.160 --> 27:08.963
[Director] Do not forget,
Yuta Okkotsu's execution

27:09.096 --> 27:11.533
has only been
temporarily suspended.

27:11.665 --> 27:13.200
And don't you forget

27:14.201 --> 27:16.971
that if it comes down
to that decision,

27:17.104 --> 27:19.173
I'll side with Yuta Okkotsu.

27:20.641 --> 27:22.643
(footsteps tapping)

27:22.776 --> 27:24.178
Damn.

27:24.311 --> 27:26.615
Those school directors
are such rude old geezers.

27:26.747 --> 27:28.883
I don't ever wanna
become like them.

27:29.016 --> 27:31.785
I'll have to be careful
that I never do.

27:31.919 --> 27:33.154
Don't they get it?

27:33.287 --> 27:35.524
No one should be allowed
to take youth away

27:35.656 --> 27:36.857
from young people.

27:39.293 --> 27:42.163
(Yuta groaning)

27:44.832 --> 27:47.301
Maki and Toge,
it's your last lap.

27:48.302 --> 27:50.171
(Yuta groaning)

27:50.304 --> 27:52.306
No one will take
their youth away.

27:59.648 --> 28:02.816
(door clicks)

28:02.950 --> 28:04.385
Go in, after you.

28:04.519 --> 28:05.386
(Yuta groans)

28:05.520 --> 28:06.387
Okay.

28:11.892 --> 28:14.328
(Yuta gasps)

28:18.432 --> 28:20.935
It's nearly impossible
to exorcize a curse

28:21.068 --> 28:23.170
as big as Rika Orimoto.

28:23.304 --> 28:26.340
However, breaking the
curse is a different story.

28:26.473 --> 28:29.910
You have to identify thousands
of knots of cursed energy,

28:30.044 --> 28:32.246
and unravel them one by one.

28:33.047 --> 28:35.149
It's a method that can
only be pursued by you,

28:35.282 --> 28:37.184
the person that she's cursed.

28:37.318 --> 28:39.353
What exactly am
I supposed to do?

28:39.486 --> 28:40.888
Here, use this.

28:41.021 --> 28:41.855
(sword whooshes)

28:41.989 --> 28:43.390
(Yuta groans)

28:43.525 --> 28:45.594
Whoa, a katana?

28:45.726 --> 28:47.228
You see, curses are most stable

28:47.361 --> 28:49.263
when they're
possessing an object.

28:50.064 --> 28:51.432
If you remember,
back at that school,

28:51.566 --> 28:54.201
you used that ring
to connect to Rika.

28:54.335 --> 28:56.270
The pipeline's already there.

28:56.403 --> 28:58.906
So now you need to borrow
part of Rika's curse,

28:59.039 --> 29:01.775
imbue it into the
katana, and control it.

29:01.909 --> 29:03.877
Increase the amount
as you repeat it,

29:04.011 --> 29:05.746
and eventually you'll
have the whole curse

29:05.879 --> 29:07.248
under your control.

29:07.381 --> 29:09.383
Once you do that,
then you're free.

29:11.018 --> 29:13.420
Both you and her.

29:14.955 --> 29:17.324
Imbue the curse into the katana.

29:17.458 --> 29:19.126
But that's not all.

29:19.260 --> 29:21.696
You also have to learn
how to wield a blade.

29:22.396 --> 29:24.465
Until you can combine
those two skills,

29:24.599 --> 29:26.133
you'll still be weak.

29:26.267 --> 29:29.303
So the first thing we're gonna
do is to get you training.

29:33.807 --> 29:36.410
(upbeat music)

29:49.490 --> 29:50.659
(Yuta grunts)

29:50.791 --> 29:55.462
- (Maki and Yuta grunting)
- (sword stick thudding)

29:58.465 --> 30:00.367
(Maki and Yuta grunting)

30:00.502 --> 30:02.169
Oh, nice.

30:02.303 --> 30:07.509
- (Maki and Yuta grunting)
- (sword stick thudding)

30:20.487 --> 30:21.822
What's up?

30:21.955 --> 30:23.658
How's it going?

30:23.792 --> 30:24.858
Oh, It's going.

30:24.992 --> 30:26.126
(Yuta grunts)

30:26.260 --> 30:28.128
Don't get distracted, newbie.

30:28.996 --> 30:30.264
Yeah, right.

30:30.397 --> 30:32.366
[Maki] Don't just stand
there, take your stance.

30:32.499 --> 30:33.467
Idiot.

30:33.601 --> 30:34.602
Sorry.

30:35.436 --> 30:37.971
Are you gonna land a
blow sometime today?

30:39.808 --> 30:41.308
Yeah, right now.

30:42.476 --> 30:44.546
(upbeat music)

30:44.679 --> 30:50.050
- (Maki and Yuta grunting)
- (sword stick thudding)

30:56.890 --> 30:58.258
She dodged that?

30:58.959 --> 31:00.528
But now she's off-balance.

31:00.662 --> 31:02.162
I'll get her on the landing.

31:03.665 --> 31:04.498
(stick whooshes)

31:04.632 --> 31:05.933
No way.

31:06.066 --> 31:09.069
(Maki and Yuta grunting)

31:09.203 --> 31:10.070
- (Maki grunts)
- (stick thuds)

31:10.204 --> 31:11.506
Congrats, you're dead.

31:12.473 --> 31:14.241
I win again, and
remain undefeated.

31:14.375 --> 31:16.511
Was that last part necessary?

31:16.644 --> 31:18.045
Don't be so soft.

31:18.178 --> 31:20.849
You should always treat training
like it's a real battle.

31:20.981 --> 31:22.584
Both experiencing
pain and avoiding pain

31:22.717 --> 31:25.352
makes a huge difference
in how fast you grow.

31:26.621 --> 31:29.923
She's right, I gotta
get back in there.

31:30.759 --> 31:31.959
One more, please.

31:32.761 --> 31:34.194
I have to get better.

31:35.362 --> 31:38.932
If I don't improve, I'll
never break Rika's curse.

31:40.234 --> 31:42.202
- (Maki and Yuta grunting)
- (sword stick thudding)

31:42.336 --> 31:45.339
It's been three months since
Yuta came to Jujutsu High.

31:45.472 --> 31:47.876
His movements are
getting better every day.

31:48.008 --> 31:49.309
[Toge] Salmon.

31:49.443 --> 31:51.579
Even his personality
is more positive now.

31:51.713 --> 31:53.013
[Toge] Salmon roe.

31:53.147 --> 31:55.315
And Maki looks like she's
having more fun too.

31:55.449 --> 31:58.686
I don't think she got to spar
very often with other weapon.

31:59.721 --> 32:00.588
(Panda gasps)

32:00.722 --> 32:02.791
I've had a revelation.

32:02.923 --> 32:04.526
Hey, Yuta.

32:04.659 --> 32:05.527
Come here.

32:05.660 --> 32:06.795
Come over here.

32:06.927 --> 32:08.596
Huh?

32:08.730 --> 32:10.097
What's up, Panda?

32:10.230 --> 32:11.833
We have to have a super
important discussion,

32:11.965 --> 32:13.535
so listen close.

32:13.668 --> 32:16.937
What do you like better,
big or small boobs?

32:17.070 --> 32:18.573
What?

32:18.706 --> 32:19.973
To tell you the truth,

32:20.107 --> 32:20.941
I've never given it
much thought before.

32:21.074 --> 32:22.744
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

32:23.277 --> 32:25.580
I guess given the choice
I like them somewhat big?

32:25.713 --> 32:27.615
Oh, really?

32:27.749 --> 32:29.517
Maki.

32:29.651 --> 32:30.552
Huh?

32:30.685 --> 32:32.620
You have a shot.

32:32.754 --> 32:35.088
Shot, shot, shot.

32:36.423 --> 32:37.759
[Maki] What crazy
ideas are you getting

32:37.892 --> 32:38.760
in that head of yours?

32:38.893 --> 32:40.194
[Panda] Don't be so shy.

32:40.327 --> 32:42.095
It's not like you're
in elementary school.

32:42.229 --> 32:43.430
[Maki] Oh, that's it.

32:43.565 --> 32:45.065
- I'm gonna kill you.
- (Yuta giggles)

32:45.199 --> 32:45.999
- What're they fighting about?
- [Panda] Ow, ow.

32:46.133 --> 32:47.334
[Toge] Kelp.

32:48.636 --> 32:51.606
(Yuta giggles)

32:51.739 --> 32:55.342
[Yuta] I still don't understand
anything Inumaki says.

32:55.476 --> 32:57.946
Which makes me a
little scared of him.

32:58.078 --> 32:58.947
(Gojo claps)

32:59.079 --> 33:01.783
Okay, gather round.

33:01.916 --> 33:05.653
You two continue training or
whatever it is you're doing.

33:06.588 --> 33:08.590
Toge, you've been
requested for a curse

33:08.723 --> 33:09.958
that you're perfect for.

33:10.090 --> 33:11.726
Shouldn't take you
long to exorcize it.

33:11.860 --> 33:12.727
[Toge] Salmon.

33:12.861 --> 33:14.394
Requested?

33:14.529 --> 33:16.598
Toge is the only grade-two
sorcerer among us first-years.

33:16.731 --> 33:19.366
He's allowed to take on
missions all on his own.

33:19.501 --> 33:20.702
(Panda and Maki grunts)

33:20.835 --> 33:22.035
Wow, that's impressive.

33:22.169 --> 33:23.270
[Maki] Your
special-grade's higher.

33:23.403 --> 33:25.138
Yuta, why don't
you go along too.

33:25.272 --> 33:26.808
You'll be Toge's support.

33:26.941 --> 33:27.876
Huh?

33:28.008 --> 33:29.476
You want me to support him?

33:29.611 --> 33:32.312
[Satoru] Well, you'll be more
like an observer, really.

33:32.446 --> 33:34.481
There's a wide
variety of jujutsu,

33:34.616 --> 33:36.450
so you can assume
there are as many ways

33:36.584 --> 33:39.386
to exorcize a curse as
there are sorcerers.

33:39.521 --> 33:42.155
Toge's cursed speech is a
good example of one way.

33:42.289 --> 33:43.758
Make sure to learn from him.

33:43.892 --> 33:45.392
Cursed speech?

33:45.527 --> 33:48.161
As the term suggests, it's
imbuing speech with curses.

33:48.295 --> 33:50.865
Eh, it'll make sense
once you see it.

33:50.999 --> 33:54.536
To break a curse, you must
first understand curses.

33:55.904 --> 33:57.772
[Yuta] My first real mission.

33:57.906 --> 33:59.874
No, wait, my second.

34:00.008 --> 34:02.175
Oh, I'm still so nervous.

34:03.678 --> 34:04.679
[Toge] Salmon.

34:04.812 --> 34:06.113
(Yuta groans)

34:06.246 --> 34:07.114
Oh, I.

34:07.247 --> 34:08.115
You startled me.

34:08.248 --> 34:09.449
Sorry.

34:10.217 --> 34:12.687
Yuta, one more thing.

34:12.820 --> 34:13.755
Coming.

34:13.888 --> 34:15.289
Sorry, but I don't have the time

34:15.422 --> 34:16.991
to supervise this mission.

34:17.124 --> 34:20.562
But this job is typically one
Toge could handle by himself.

34:20.695 --> 34:21.996
So you can relax.

34:22.129 --> 34:24.732
There's only one thing that
you need to be careful of.

34:26.000 --> 34:27.535
Don't let Rika out.

34:28.836 --> 34:30.705
There's no guarantee
she'll go back in,

34:30.838 --> 34:32.205
like she did last time.

34:32.339 --> 34:34.042
Only use the portion
of Rika's power

34:34.174 --> 34:36.076
that you can imbue
in your sword.

34:37.545 --> 34:40.882
Do you know what will happen
if you let her out again?

34:41.015 --> 34:41.916
No, what happens?

34:42.050 --> 34:44.719
Bluh, both you and me.

34:44.852 --> 34:46.386
Dead as a door nail.

34:46.521 --> 34:47.722
I'm counting on you.

34:47.855 --> 34:49.958
(Yuta groans)

34:50.090 --> 34:53.160
[Yuta] Why does he have to
bring that up right now?

34:59.033 --> 35:01.569
(crows caw)

35:04.539 --> 35:07.842
(car engine revving)

35:10.745 --> 35:11.746
We've arrived.

35:13.815 --> 35:15.349
Hapina Shopping District.

35:15.482 --> 35:18.620
At the moment, most of the
stores are closed to the public.

35:19.687 --> 35:22.824
"There's a project to demolish
the Hapina Shopping District

35:22.957 --> 35:24.592
in order to put up a new mall.

35:24.726 --> 35:26.561
During an inspection
of the area,

35:26.694 --> 35:28.796
we confirmed a pack
of low-level curses

35:28.930 --> 35:30.798
hiding among the corridors.

35:32.066 --> 35:33.333
In order to exorcize them,

35:33.467 --> 35:36.203
we request, grade-two
sorcerer, Toge."

35:36.336 --> 35:37.672
Huh, wait.

35:37.805 --> 35:39.339
Where did Toge go?

35:39.473 --> 35:40.407
He was right here.

35:40.541 --> 35:41.809
[Man] Thank you, come again.

35:41.943 --> 35:44.277
Oh, Mr. Ijichi, over there.

35:46.246 --> 35:48.049
He was shopping?

35:48.181 --> 35:49.917
What did you buy in that store?

35:52.687 --> 35:53.821
Throat medicine?

35:54.889 --> 35:56.189
(Ijichi sighs)

35:56.323 --> 35:57.959
In short, they want
us to exorcize it now

35:58.092 --> 36:00.662
before the building they're
spending so much money on

36:00.795 --> 36:03.163
develops a reputation
for cursed energy.

36:03.296 --> 36:04.699
[Toge] Salmon.

36:04.832 --> 36:05.867
Now then.

36:06.000 --> 36:07.401
I will draw the veil.

36:08.368 --> 36:09.570
Good luck to you.

36:14.642 --> 36:17.879
(Yuta breathes deeply)

36:20.715 --> 36:23.985
He said, it was a pack
of low-level curses.

36:24.118 --> 36:25.419
[Toge] Pollack roe.

36:25.553 --> 36:28.756
(footsteps tapping)

36:42.770 --> 36:45.006
[Fish Curse] That's
not fair, Mama.

36:45.139 --> 36:47.909
My brother got more than I did.

36:48.042 --> 36:49.309
[Fish Curse] So what?

36:49.443 --> 36:51.179
Let's trade doubles that
way we both get one.

36:51.311 --> 36:54.782
(fish curse chattering)

36:58.653 --> 37:00.722
[Fish Curse] Is
the cheapest stuff.

37:01.656 --> 37:03.290
[Maki] The weaker curses are,

37:03.423 --> 37:05.026
the more they group together.

37:05.159 --> 37:06.694
Look at them all.

37:06.828 --> 37:08.930
Weak or not, there's
just too many.

37:14.068 --> 37:15.268
Huh?

37:15.402 --> 37:16.604
Inumaki?

37:17.205 --> 37:18.072
It's dangerous.

37:18.206 --> 37:19.807
Don't get too close.

37:19.941 --> 37:20.942
Explode.

37:23.578 --> 37:26.614
(explosion booms)

37:28.116 --> 37:29.249
Oh, wow.

37:29.382 --> 37:31.886
So this is cursed speech?

37:32.019 --> 37:32.887
Huh?

37:33.020 --> 37:34.856
Oh, it's over already?

37:35.990 --> 37:37.058
[Toge] Tuna mayo.

37:37.191 --> 37:38.059
(Yuta groans)

37:38.192 --> 37:39.392
[Yuta] His voice.

37:40.194 --> 37:41.294
Wait.

37:41.428 --> 37:43.430
That explains the
throat medicine.

37:44.832 --> 37:47.201
What an incredible
amount of power.

37:47.334 --> 37:50.605
But I'm sure it comes with
a great deal of risk, too.

37:53.074 --> 37:54.341
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

37:54.474 --> 37:55.710
Is something wrong?

37:56.644 --> 37:59.881
Oh, yeah, the veil
isn't lifting.

38:00.014 --> 38:02.750
Hmm, I can't get through.

38:02.884 --> 38:05.418
Does this mean,
there's no way out?

38:05.553 --> 38:06.419
(air whooshes)

38:06.554 --> 38:10.024
(Toge and Yuta groans)

38:13.027 --> 38:14.294
What is this curse?

38:14.427 --> 38:17.098
Its presence is different
from the others.

38:17.231 --> 38:18.766
[Zomba] Zomba.

38:19.867 --> 38:20.735
(Yuta groans)

38:20.868 --> 38:21.969
(explosion booms)

38:22.103 --> 38:23.303
Inumaki.

38:24.772 --> 38:25.773
Twist.

38:28.576 --> 38:30.878
(Toge groans)

38:31.012 --> 38:33.514
(Toge coughs)

38:35.116 --> 38:37.285
(ground rumbles)

38:37.417 --> 38:39.554
What in the world is that thing?

38:39.687 --> 38:42.890
(suspenseful music)

38:46.527 --> 38:48.629
They said the curses
were low-level,

38:48.763 --> 38:50.665
but that thing is enormous.

38:50.798 --> 38:52.499
This isn't what we were told.

38:53.835 --> 38:55.670
That thing is scarier
than the big guys

38:55.803 --> 38:57.839
from the elementary school.

38:57.972 --> 38:58.973
Way scarier.

38:59.106 --> 39:00.641
(Toge grunts)

39:00.775 --> 39:02.310
Inumaki, you're hurt.

39:02.442 --> 39:03.845
Where did it get you?

39:04.444 --> 39:05.313
Whoa.

39:05.445 --> 39:06.379
Twisted.

39:06.514 --> 39:07.882
Salmon.

39:08.015 --> 39:09.217
(Yuta groans)

39:09.349 --> 39:11.719
You shouldn't mess with
it, it might get worse.

39:12.220 --> 39:13.386
I'm sorry.

39:14.021 --> 39:15.556
It's all my fault.

39:23.998 --> 39:26.834
It doesn't seem to be
looking for us at all.

39:28.336 --> 39:30.805
I'll contact Mr. Ijichi.

39:30.938 --> 39:31.606
Huh?

39:31.739 --> 39:33.074
Out of service?

39:33.207 --> 39:34.575
That can't be.

39:34.709 --> 39:36.077
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

39:36.210 --> 39:37.078
Huh?

39:37.211 --> 39:38.613
Because of the veil?

39:40.948 --> 39:44.118
Well, if the veil won't
lift, we have to exorcize it.

39:44.252 --> 39:45.452
Isn't that right?

39:50.124 --> 39:51.125
Inumaki?

39:51.859 --> 39:53.895
You shouldn't be
moving around already.

39:55.963 --> 39:57.064
Salmon.

39:57.198 --> 39:58.199
(Toge coughs)

39:58.332 --> 39:59.533
Huh?

40:00.835 --> 40:03.170
You want to fight this
battle by yourself?

40:28.162 --> 40:29.997
Thanks, Inumaki.

40:30.131 --> 40:31.132
But,

40:33.701 --> 40:35.503
I'm going to come with you.

40:40.141 --> 40:42.143
(footsteps tapping)

40:42.276 --> 40:43.476
We'll both do our best.

40:43.611 --> 40:44.979
Let's go.

40:45.112 --> 40:48.082
(suspenseful music)

40:54.088 --> 40:56.590
(Zomba growls)

40:57.425 --> 41:00.127
[Rika] Go get him, Yuta.

41:00.261 --> 41:02.763
(Zomba growl)

41:04.932 --> 41:06.834
Hey, what's it mad at me for?

41:06.968 --> 41:09.804
Like it wasn't scary enough.

41:09.937 --> 41:10.938
Huh?

41:12.406 --> 41:15.643
(Yuta breathes deeply)

41:15.776 --> 41:17.511
Don't take your eyes off him.

41:17.645 --> 41:19.447
Don't stop moving.

41:19.580 --> 41:21.949
Imbue the curse into the katana.

41:26.287 --> 41:28.022
(sword clanging)

41:28.155 --> 41:31.192
(explosion booms)

41:34.595 --> 41:36.330
(Yuta grunts)

41:36.464 --> 41:39.100
(explosion booms)

41:39.233 --> 41:41.802
Inumaki has an
incredibly kind heart.

41:41.936 --> 41:43.938
He doesn't want to
accidentally curse others,

41:44.071 --> 41:46.474
so he speaks in rice
ball ingredients,

41:46.607 --> 41:48.976
words that can't carry curses.

41:49.110 --> 41:50.978
Even today, he helped me out.

41:51.112 --> 41:53.114
He tried to keep me
away from danger.

41:54.415 --> 41:56.717
Earlier, when I was
totally freaking out,

41:56.851 --> 41:59.220
he was trying to make
me feel comfortable.

42:01.222 --> 42:04.258
(explosion booms)

42:06.327 --> 42:07.161
(Zomba groans)

42:07.294 --> 42:09.063
(sword whooshing)

42:09.196 --> 42:10.498
(Zomba groans)

42:10.631 --> 42:12.199
A superficial wound.

42:12.333 --> 42:13.701
Boy, he's tough.

42:13.834 --> 42:15.903
- (explosion booms)
- (Yuta grunts)

42:16.037 --> 42:19.240
Okay, maybe I can't compete
with this curse but Inumaki can.

42:21.375 --> 42:24.078
(suspenseful music)

42:24.211 --> 42:25.346
Inumaki, catch.

42:25.479 --> 42:27.081
(throat medicine whooshes)

42:27.214 --> 42:30.851
I'm not gonna let Inumaki
kindness go to waste.

42:31.585 --> 42:32.853
Nice catch.

42:37.691 --> 42:38.559
(Toge gulps)

42:38.692 --> 42:39.693
(Zomba groans)

42:39.827 --> 42:42.596
(upbeat music)

42:44.265 --> 42:47.268
(explosion booms)

42:49.570 --> 42:50.905
Get crushed.

42:54.208 --> 42:56.877
(blood splashes)

42:58.379 --> 42:59.480
Incredible.

42:59.613 --> 43:00.915
[Toge] Mustard leaf.

43:03.250 --> 43:04.585
[Yuta] Oh, I'm fine.

43:04.718 --> 43:05.920
It's only a scratch.

43:09.156 --> 43:10.157
[Toge] Salmon.

43:12.561 --> 43:14.795
Yeah, good work.

43:18.432 --> 43:20.201
Once I break Rika's curse,

43:20.334 --> 43:22.736
I'm gonna be a
normal person again.

43:23.737 --> 43:26.407
I won't be able to stay
at Jujutsu High anymore,

43:26.541 --> 43:30.244
but until then, I'm gonna
try to help as many people

43:30.377 --> 43:31.378
as I can.

43:33.280 --> 43:34.215
(Yuta groans)

43:34.348 --> 43:36.317
We still can't
get out, can't we?

43:37.451 --> 43:38.886
What a shame.

43:39.019 --> 43:42.256
I came here just to see the
rumored curse named Rika.

43:43.290 --> 43:46.961
As a special-grade, I was
hoping to meet her soon.

43:49.430 --> 43:52.099
Perhaps, I should go
return this to him.

44:00.207 --> 44:02.977
Toge's been able to use cursed
speech since he was born.

44:03.110 --> 44:05.412
You can imagine when he
was just a little boy,

44:05.547 --> 44:08.617
he struggled quite a bit with
his new cursed speech power.

44:08.749 --> 44:10.985
Sometimes he accidentally
cursed people

44:11.118 --> 44:12.486
that he didn't mean to.

44:12.621 --> 44:16.090
In fact, his situation was
pretty similar to yours.

44:16.223 --> 44:17.825
That's why he's been
worried about you

44:17.958 --> 44:20.361
ever since the day you
transferred in here.

44:21.495 --> 44:25.166
It's easy to misunderstand
him, but he's a good guy.

44:25.866 --> 44:28.936
Try to be as kind to
him as he is to you.

44:29.470 --> 44:30.337
Mm, I will.

44:30.471 --> 44:31.540
(Yuta grunts)

44:31.672 --> 44:32.773
Time to start our
morning training.

44:32.907 --> 44:33.974
- (Panda giggles)
- Okay, I'm coming.

44:34.108 --> 44:35.809
Panda, what are you laughing at?

44:35.943 --> 44:37.178
Something funny?

44:37.311 --> 44:38.279
[Panda] Well,

44:38.412 --> 44:40.314
- not really, but.
- Hey, Maki, hold on.

44:40.447 --> 44:41.682
Huh?

44:41.815 --> 44:43.518
Are there any cool
tricks you can teach me?

44:43.652 --> 44:46.887
I'd like to imbue my curse
into my katana more smoothly.

44:47.021 --> 44:48.155
Just forget it.

44:48.289 --> 44:50.291
Don't ask me about
cursed energy.

44:54.161 --> 44:55.162
Hmm?

44:57.431 --> 45:00.467
After scouring every inch of
the Hapina Shopping District,

45:00.602 --> 45:03.170
I found three different
types of residuals.

45:03.304 --> 45:04.838
Mr. Ijichi doesn't
think it's likely

45:04.972 --> 45:06.675
we're going to find
anything more than that

45:06.807 --> 45:07.676
if we keep looking.

45:07.808 --> 45:09.376
Okay, got it, thanks.

45:09.511 --> 45:10.579
Excellent report.

45:10.711 --> 45:11.912
You bet.

45:16.016 --> 45:18.886
(Satoru sniffs)

45:22.089 --> 45:25.292
(suspenseful music)

45:27.662 --> 45:30.864
(footsteps tapping)

45:43.477 --> 45:44.478
Sorry to bother you.

45:45.246 --> 45:48.382
Our inspection showed, that
someone lowered a second veil

45:48.516 --> 45:49.718
on top of my own.

45:49.850 --> 45:51.118
We don't know who yet,

45:51.252 --> 45:53.287
but we're analyzing
the residual energy.

45:53.420 --> 45:54.689
In addition,

45:54.822 --> 45:57.525
a semi-first-grade curse made
an unexpected appearance.

45:58.826 --> 46:01.895
It's my fault for not being
as thorough as I should have.

46:02.029 --> 46:03.397
I'll accept any punishment.

46:03.531 --> 46:04.599
No, you're fine.

46:04.733 --> 46:06.767
You were just outclassed.

46:06.900 --> 46:08.802
Outclassed by who?

46:08.936 --> 46:11.438
Do you have an idea
about who did it?

46:11.573 --> 46:14.775
(suspenseful music)

46:26.920 --> 46:28.289
Suguru Geto.

46:30.424 --> 46:33.160
A special-grade
jujutsu sorcerer.

46:33.294 --> 46:35.896
One of four who was
banished from Jujutsu High.

46:36.531 --> 46:39.933
He cursed over a hundred
normal people to death.

46:40.067 --> 46:41.468
The worst curse user ever.

46:55.316 --> 46:57.585
Mom, I'll be fine,
let's go home.

46:57.719 --> 47:00.354
We're already here, let's
just wait a little longer

47:00.487 --> 47:01.889
so we can meet him.

47:02.022 --> 47:02.923
But, Mom.

47:03.057 --> 47:03.891
(door whooshes)

47:04.024 --> 47:06.528
(both groans)

47:18.540 --> 47:19.940
Hello, Ladies.

47:20.074 --> 47:22.510
As I understand it, you said
your daughter was being haunted

47:22.644 --> 47:23.977
by a ghost.

47:24.111 --> 47:26.347
Isn't that right, Mrs. Sato?

47:26.480 --> 47:30.752
Ah, yeah, but it's
Saito, actually.

47:30.884 --> 47:33.153
No, your name is Mrs. Sato.

47:33.287 --> 47:36.423
I've decided Sato is a
better name than Saito.

47:37.525 --> 47:39.193
(mom groans)

47:39.326 --> 47:41.195
Come on, mom, let's just go.

47:41.328 --> 47:43.897
Sweetheart, let's get
this problem taken care of

47:44.031 --> 47:45.165
once and for all.

47:45.299 --> 47:46.668
This whole thing
seems shady, though.

47:46.801 --> 47:49.903
You constantly feel a
piercing gaze upon you.

47:51.038 --> 47:52.473
Sometimes your
shoulders feel heavy,

47:52.607 --> 47:55.175
and it becomes
difficult to breathe.

47:55.309 --> 47:57.512
Almost as if you've
forgotten how.

47:58.780 --> 48:02.517
And you often dream that
you're being assaulted.

48:04.318 --> 48:05.553
How did you know that?

48:07.756 --> 48:09.390
Try not to move.

48:09.524 --> 48:12.226
(monster groans)

48:20.000 --> 48:22.403
Wait, no way.

48:22.537 --> 48:23.571
It feels better.

48:26.473 --> 48:29.677
Honestly, I don't know how
we could ever repay you.

48:30.779 --> 48:32.079
Don't worry.

48:32.212 --> 48:34.114
We should all help
those in times of need.

48:34.248 --> 48:36.785
Come on by if you
have any more trouble.

48:36.917 --> 48:38.085
(both giggles)

48:38.218 --> 48:39.521
See, I told you so.

48:39.654 --> 48:41.989
What this man has done
for you is simply godly.

48:42.122 --> 48:43.323
Yeah.

48:43.858 --> 48:45.325
Godly, huh?

48:45.459 --> 48:48.395
That Mrs. Sato is a
smart one, isn't she?

48:49.296 --> 48:51.999
Filthy monkey who
can't even use jujutsu.

48:52.132 --> 48:54.468
Your true feelings seem
to be showing, Geto.

48:54.602 --> 48:56.604
The leaders are all
waiting for you.

48:56.738 --> 48:58.138
They're in the meeting room.

48:59.306 --> 49:01.676
What is that stuff you're
spraying everywhere?

49:01.810 --> 49:03.444
Disinfecting deodorant.

49:03.578 --> 49:06.614
I don't want everyone to
breathe in the monkey smell.

49:07.882 --> 49:09.584
What a great day.

49:09.717 --> 49:10.819
I'm so happy.

49:10.951 --> 49:12.554
It's been so long
since we all met.

49:12.687 --> 49:14.656
I know, since all
the leaders are here,

49:14.789 --> 49:16.190
let's take a photo together.

49:16.323 --> 49:17.191
Where's my camera?

49:17.324 --> 49:18.526
Got it right here.

49:18.660 --> 49:20.929
- (camera shutter clicks)
- (Suda giggles)

49:21.061 --> 49:22.029
Geto.

49:22.162 --> 49:24.566
I want to see Geto right now.

49:24.699 --> 49:25.499
(Kanamori groans)

49:25.633 --> 49:27.100
Geto, damn you.

49:27.234 --> 49:28.101
(Kanamori groans)

49:28.235 --> 49:29.571
If it isn't Mr. Kanamori.

49:29.704 --> 49:32.105
What brings you here
in such a sweaty panic?

49:32.239 --> 49:35.275
Don't play dumb, hurry
up and exorcize my curse.

49:35.409 --> 49:37.946
Do you know how much
I've paid you already?

49:38.078 --> 49:38.947
(Kanamori grunts)

49:39.079 --> 49:40.047
How much?

49:40.180 --> 49:42.216
Approximately 105 million yen.

49:42.349 --> 49:45.385
However, no donations
for the past six months.

49:45.520 --> 49:47.655
[Suguru] I guess
that's it for you then.

49:47.789 --> 49:48.656
Wait a minute.

49:48.790 --> 49:51.626
(Kanamori groans)

49:52.794 --> 49:54.027
There are lots of monkeys,

49:54.161 --> 49:56.463
and they all have
their own role to play.

49:56.598 --> 49:58.700
There are
money-collecting monkeys

49:58.833 --> 50:00.969
and curse-collecting monkeys.

50:01.101 --> 50:02.837
You happen to be the former.

50:02.971 --> 50:06.240
If you're out of money, I
have no further use for you.

50:07.307 --> 50:08.175
(Suguru gulps)

50:08.308 --> 50:09.176
(Suguru snaps)

50:09.309 --> 50:11.011
Screw you then.

50:11.144 --> 50:14.481
[Monster] Suck, suck,
suck, suck, suck.

50:14.616 --> 50:17.417
Suck, suck, suck, suck, suck.

50:18.786 --> 50:20.822
Suck, suck, suck.

50:20.955 --> 50:23.691
(blood splashes)

50:25.827 --> 50:27.194
Totally disgusting.

50:27.327 --> 50:29.931
I can't believe he's
part of the same species.

50:30.063 --> 50:31.633
Now you know why
I'm always saying

50:31.766 --> 50:33.801
that they're
nothing but monkeys.

50:34.636 --> 50:37.437
The time is here,
my beloved family.

50:37.572 --> 50:39.641
Let's lower the curtain
on the age of monkeys,

50:39.774 --> 50:43.545
and build a paradise
for jujutsu sorcerers.

50:43.678 --> 50:46.179
First though, we must
destroy the cornerstone

50:46.313 --> 50:49.684
of the jujutsu world,
Jujutsu High School.

50:51.819 --> 50:52.854
(Yuta groans)

50:52.987 --> 50:54.656
[Panda] What's wrong, Yuta?

50:54.789 --> 50:55.990
Well.

50:56.123 --> 50:57.859
I think I just had
a bad premonition.

50:57.992 --> 51:00.127
- You're imagining things.
- Yep, he's imagining things.

51:00.260 --> 51:01.729
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

51:01.863 --> 51:02.864
(Yuta groans)

51:02.997 --> 51:04.364
[Yuta] Guys, wait up.

51:04.498 --> 51:05.800
[Panda] I hate to
tell you, Yuta,

51:05.934 --> 51:08.201
but your ability to sense
cursed energy sucks.

51:08.335 --> 51:09.469
[Maki] I figured it's dulled,

51:09.604 --> 51:10.905
with something like
Rika inside you.

51:11.039 --> 51:12.239
[Toge] Tuna.

51:13.641 --> 51:16.476
We still aren't picking up
on any actions from Geto.

51:16.611 --> 51:19.547
Are you sure you're not
worrying over him for nothing?

51:19.681 --> 51:22.684
Principal, it pains me to
tell you that's not possible.

51:22.817 --> 51:25.587
I confirmed it
myself on the scene.

51:25.720 --> 51:27.487
There's no way I would
mistake the residuals

51:27.622 --> 51:30.257
of Suguru Geto's cursed energy.

51:30.390 --> 51:32.727
Hmm, Suguru.

51:34.261 --> 51:35.429
God damn it.

51:35.563 --> 51:37.497
Speaking of that little devil.

51:37.632 --> 51:41.002
Gather all sorcerers on campus,
semi-first-grade and above.

51:41.134 --> 51:42.870
In the circle out
front, right now.

51:44.038 --> 51:45.405
That's unusual.

51:45.540 --> 51:47.709
I guess Yuta was
right, after all.

51:47.842 --> 51:48.710
[Toge] Salmon.

51:48.843 --> 51:49.811
Huh?

51:50.277 --> 51:53.180
(wings whooshes)

51:57.585 --> 52:00.722
Sorry bird brain but
you're in the wrong nest.

52:00.855 --> 52:02.657
I haven't seen
that curse before.

52:02.790 --> 52:03.825
Salmon roe.

52:03.958 --> 52:06.426
Wow, that's a real big bird.

52:06.561 --> 52:09.097
This place never
does change, does it.

52:09.229 --> 52:10.397
Yuck.

52:10.531 --> 52:11.933
Mr. Geto, please
don't tell me this is

52:12.066 --> 52:13.166
what Tokyo looks like?

52:13.300 --> 52:15.103
Feels like we're
out in the sticks.

52:15.235 --> 52:16.938
Nanako, that's rude.

52:17.071 --> 52:18.171
What?

52:18.305 --> 52:19.641
You know you think
so, too, Mimiko.

52:19.774 --> 52:22.110
Come on, get out
of there already.

52:22.242 --> 52:23.778
Aren't you cold without a shirt?

52:23.911 --> 52:25.145
Hey, who are those guys?

52:25.278 --> 52:27.048
Whoa, it's a panda.

52:27.180 --> 52:28.116
How cute.

52:28.248 --> 52:29.684
And who are you supposed to be?

52:29.817 --> 52:32.452
Get off the school grounds
before Yuta makes you.

52:32.587 --> 52:34.354
- Pollack roe.
- Huh?

52:34.488 --> 52:37.491
Better go home before you
get beat up, by Yuta, I mean.

52:37.625 --> 52:38.593
Huh?

52:39.594 --> 52:41.829
[Suguru] Nice to meet
you, Yuta Okkotsu.

52:41.963 --> 52:43.598
My name is Suguru Geto.

52:43.731 --> 52:45.499
[Maki And Panda] He's fast.

52:46.100 --> 52:46.968
Hi.

52:47.101 --> 52:48.603
It's nice to meet you.

52:48.736 --> 52:51.673
I see you're in possession
of a truly wonderful power.

52:52.740 --> 52:56.309
And I believe, that such
great power ought to be used

52:56.443 --> 52:58.478
to create great opportunities.

52:58.613 --> 53:00.848
Have you ever questioned the
current state of the world

53:00.982 --> 53:03.383
where jujutsu
sorcerers act in secret

53:03.518 --> 53:05.920
to protect the order
of commonplace society.

53:06.054 --> 53:07.454
Hmm?

53:07.588 --> 53:10.124
You see, my friend, there's
this established paradox

53:10.290 --> 53:13.795
that mistakenly says the strong
must accommodate the weak.

53:15.228 --> 53:17.799
It's so deplorable.

53:17.932 --> 53:19.232
Okay.

53:19.366 --> 53:21.334
It's as if the apex of
all creation decided

53:21.468 --> 53:23.370
to halt its own
path of evolution.

53:23.504 --> 53:24.972
It's nonsense.

53:25.106 --> 53:27.374
And it's time for mankind
to reconsider its strategy

53:27.508 --> 53:28.943
for survival.

53:29.077 --> 53:33.447
Which is exactly why we
would like you to help us.

53:33.581 --> 53:34.882
Help you with what?

53:35.850 --> 53:37.652
We're going to kill
all non-sorcerers,

53:37.785 --> 53:40.555
and create a world
of jujutsu sorcerers.

53:41.923 --> 53:42.790
[Maki] What?

53:42.924 --> 53:44.759
[Panda] Is he serious?

53:44.892 --> 53:46.127
(Toge grunts)

53:46.259 --> 53:47.260
[Satoru] Do me a favor.

53:47.394 --> 53:48.830
Hmm?

53:48.963 --> 53:50.230
Could you please stop
preaching your crazy beliefs

53:50.363 --> 53:51.566
to my students?

53:54.202 --> 53:56.571
Satoru, long time no see.

53:56.704 --> 53:59.941
Step away from those
kids right now, Suguru.

54:02.210 --> 54:05.146
I heard this new first-year
class is simply outstanding.

54:05.278 --> 54:06.379
Seems it's true.

54:06.514 --> 54:08.649
You still have an
eye for talent.

54:08.783 --> 54:12.587
A special-grade cursed human,
a cursed corpse mutation,

54:12.720 --> 54:14.722
a cursed speech user.

54:14.856 --> 54:18.325
And last, the Zen'in
clan's biggest failure.

54:18.458 --> 54:19.326
(Maki groans)

54:19.459 --> 54:20.595
You piece of shit.

54:20.728 --> 54:22.496
You better watch
that mouth of yours.

54:22.630 --> 54:25.298
Because I don't need any
monkeys like you in the world

54:25.432 --> 54:26.834
that I'm creating.

54:30.470 --> 54:31.939
I'm sorry.

54:32.073 --> 54:35.643
I don't really understand
anything you're talking about

54:36.778 --> 54:40.915
but I can't help anyone
who insults my friends.

54:41.048 --> 54:42.950
So count me out.

54:43.084 --> 54:44.252
(Suguru sighs)

54:44.384 --> 54:45.820
My apologies.

54:45.953 --> 54:47.955
I didn't come here to
insult you, or your friends.

54:48.089 --> 54:49.322
That's good to know.

54:49.456 --> 54:51.526
Then why exactly
did you come here?

54:53.060 --> 54:54.996
I came to declare war.

54:56.130 --> 54:58.599
Everyone gathered here today.

54:58.733 --> 55:02.335
I want you all to open your
ears and listen closely.

55:02.469 --> 55:05.673
On December 24th,
when the sun sets,

55:05.807 --> 55:08.976
we shall begin the Night
Parade of a Hundred Demons.

55:09.110 --> 55:10.343
(Yaga grunts)

55:10.477 --> 55:14.715
At the crucible of
curses, Shinjuku, Tokyo,

55:15.650 --> 55:18.953
as well as the holy
land of jujutsu, Kyoto.

55:19.086 --> 55:22.523
A thousand curses will be
unleashed upon each place.

55:22.657 --> 55:25.092
All with the command massacre.

55:25.226 --> 55:27.795
If you wish to avoid a
scene straight from hell,

55:27.929 --> 55:29.831
come to your best to stop it.

55:31.065 --> 55:35.136
Let us freely curse
each other to the death.

55:35.269 --> 55:38.471
(suspenseful music)

55:40.608 --> 55:41.843
(Nanako shouts)

55:41.976 --> 55:42.977
Mr. Geto.

55:43.110 --> 55:45.012
The cafe is gonna close.

55:45.146 --> 55:46.814
Oh, is it that late already?

55:46.948 --> 55:48.683
You know how it is, don't you?

55:48.816 --> 55:51.252
These girls just have to
get their favorite crepes

55:51.384 --> 55:53.054
from Takeshita Street.

55:53.187 --> 55:54.222
Come on, hurry up.

55:54.354 --> 55:55.823
I'll be taking my leave now.

55:55.957 --> 55:57.992
Nanago, I really don't
see what's so good

55:58.125 --> 56:00.061
about a place with
so many monkeys.

56:00.194 --> 56:02.763
You didn't think we'd
just let you leave?

56:04.131 --> 56:05.800
Careful, Suturu.

56:05.933 --> 56:08.703
(monster grunts)

56:10.638 --> 56:13.574
(monster growls)

56:13.708 --> 56:16.244
Your precious students
are well within my range.

56:16.376 --> 56:18.913
(monsters growling)

56:19.046 --> 56:20.014
Goodbye everybody.

56:20.147 --> 56:21.582
See you at the war.

56:23.117 --> 56:25.887
(wings whooshes)

56:35.395 --> 56:37.098
[Suguru] Survival
of the weakest.

56:37.231 --> 56:39.867
That's the proper form
society should take.

56:40.001 --> 56:43.137
Help the weak, and
discourage the strong.

56:43.271 --> 56:44.705
Listen, Satoru.

56:44.839 --> 56:48.475
Sorcerers exist to
protect non-sorcerers.

56:48.609 --> 56:50.244
[Satoru] That's your argument?

56:50.378 --> 56:52.079
God, I hate righteousness.

56:55.883 --> 56:57.652
Do you think that
you're the strongest

56:57.785 --> 56:59.887
because you're Satoru Gojo?

57:00.021 --> 57:02.890
Or are you Satoru Gojo
because you're the strongest?

57:03.024 --> 57:04.926
What exactly are
you trying to say?

57:05.059 --> 57:07.228
If I could switch
places with you

57:07.361 --> 57:09.130
then wouldn't my foolish ideals

57:09.263 --> 57:11.098
become reasonable possibilities?

57:14.702 --> 57:16.837
My path leads elsewhere.

57:16.971 --> 57:20.074
And I plan on following it
to the best of my ability.

57:21.575 --> 57:24.578
(dramatic music)

57:59.914 --> 58:02.183
Suguru Geto, a
special-grade curse user

58:02.316 --> 58:04.785
who uses cursed
spirit manipulation.

58:04.919 --> 58:06.454
Able to draw in and manipulate

58:06.587 --> 58:08.522
naturally occurring
unbound curses.

58:08.656 --> 58:09.857
That's his skill.

58:11.125 --> 58:12.326
It seems he's recently
established

58:12.460 --> 58:13.928
a new religious group

58:14.061 --> 58:16.731
so that curses can be
collected from its followers.

58:16.864 --> 58:19.433
This explains the recent
decline in reported curses.

58:19.567 --> 58:22.703
He already possessed a
significant number of curses,

58:22.837 --> 58:25.239
and it's for certain
he now has a lot more.

58:26.140 --> 58:27.942
He claims to possess
2,000 of them

58:28.075 --> 58:29.844
and that may not be a bluff.

58:29.977 --> 58:31.645
But statistically,
most of them have got

58:31.779 --> 58:34.181
to be weaker grade-two
curses or below.

58:34.315 --> 58:35.850
Also estimating generously,

58:35.983 --> 58:38.185
he can't have much more
than 50 curse users.

58:38.319 --> 58:41.355
That's actually the part
that frightens me the most.

58:41.489 --> 58:42.823
I find it hard to believe

58:42.957 --> 58:45.493
that he'd want to start a
war that he couldn't win.

58:45.626 --> 58:47.228
God damn.

58:47.361 --> 58:48.562
(Yaga grunts)

58:48.696 --> 58:50.297
Put out a call for
aid to all alumni,

58:50.431 --> 58:54.235
alert the three major clans
and the Ainu Jujutsu Society.

58:54.368 --> 58:55.703
It's all-out war.

58:55.836 --> 58:58.105
And it's not just the
curses we'll exorcize,

58:58.806 --> 58:59.907
it's Geto.

59:00.041 --> 59:01.175
That muscle-brained principal

59:01.308 --> 59:03.778
must be having a
fit right about now.

59:03.911 --> 59:07.114
(suspenseful music)

59:14.121 --> 59:16.690
If we seriously tried
to kill each other,

59:16.824 --> 59:21.295
our chance of success
would be about 30%.

59:21.429 --> 59:24.533
(man grunts)

59:24.665 --> 59:26.100
(man grunts)

59:26.233 --> 59:29.870
If the Jujutsu Society
joins, barely a 20% chance.

59:31.172 --> 59:34.275
However, there is one move
that makes that slim chance

59:34.408 --> 59:36.110
of victory jump way up.

59:37.278 --> 59:39.647
Straight up to 99%.

59:39.780 --> 59:42.049
I kill Yuta Okkotsu,

59:42.183 --> 59:44.553
and obtain the special-grade
cursed apparition,

59:44.685 --> 59:46.187
Rika Orimoto.

59:47.154 --> 59:49.023
They completely bought
my bluff back there

59:49.156 --> 59:52.660
and now they're gonna give
me exactly what I want.

59:52.793 --> 59:55.296
It doesn't matter if the
cursed spirit is bound.

59:55.429 --> 59:57.598
So long as I kill its master,

59:57.731 --> 01:00:00.267
I can absorb any curse I want.

01:00:01.936 --> 01:00:03.437
The school likes
their odds of winning,

01:00:03.572 --> 01:00:06.841
so they won't play Yuta
Okkotsu as one of their cards.

01:00:06.974 --> 01:00:08.909
After all, if he unleashes Rika,

01:00:09.043 --> 01:00:10.811
she could wipe out both sides.

01:00:11.178 --> 01:00:13.914
The aim of the Night Parade
of a Hundred Demons is

01:00:14.048 --> 01:00:16.217
to get Okkotsu alone
and unprotected.

01:00:18.819 --> 01:00:23.124
Now, let's raise the
curtain on a new age.

01:00:25.326 --> 01:00:27.094
Well, I guess,

01:00:28.996 --> 01:00:31.499
something crazy is going down.

01:00:32.133 --> 01:00:33.535
- (door slams)
- (Yuta groans)

01:00:33.667 --> 01:00:34.835
- Maki.
- Huh?

01:00:34.969 --> 01:00:36.137
What are you doing here?

01:00:36.270 --> 01:00:38.072
Classes are canceled
for the week.

01:00:38.205 --> 01:00:41.008
Well, I was just
feeling kinda restless.

01:00:41.142 --> 01:00:44.111
Doesn't seem like anyone's
around in the dorms either.

01:00:44.245 --> 01:00:45.646
That's because the
second-year students

01:00:45.779 --> 01:00:47.848
were all dispatched to Kyoto.

01:00:47.982 --> 01:00:51.118
Toge's in Shinjuku with
some others as backup.

01:00:51.252 --> 01:00:53.654
And since the Principal
likes Panda so much,

01:00:53.787 --> 01:00:55.489
he's probably with Toge too.

01:00:55.624 --> 01:00:56.824
I see.

01:01:01.795 --> 01:01:03.464
- Go ahead.
- Huh?

01:01:03.598 --> 01:01:04.999
I know you wanna ask,

01:01:05.132 --> 01:01:07.636
about why Geto said
I was a failure.

01:01:07.768 --> 01:01:11.705
No, I, well, yeah.

01:01:13.642 --> 01:01:15.510
(Maki sighs)

01:01:15.644 --> 01:01:17.244
My family is the Zen'in clan.

01:01:17.378 --> 01:01:21.182
One of the three major families
of elite jujutsu sorcerers.

01:01:21.315 --> 01:01:23.717
Do you have any idea what
the minimum requirement is

01:01:23.851 --> 01:01:25.386
to be a jujutsu sorcerer?

01:01:25.520 --> 01:01:27.321
Huh, let me think.

01:01:30.024 --> 01:01:31.725
[Maki] It's being
able to see curses.

01:01:31.859 --> 01:01:33.294
Oh, yeah, right.

01:01:33.427 --> 01:01:36.665
Ordinary people, even
they sometimes see curses,

01:01:36.797 --> 01:01:39.066
like when they're
at death's door.

01:01:39.200 --> 01:01:41.001
But I can't see curses
without the help

01:01:41.135 --> 01:01:43.070
of these lame glasses.

01:01:43.204 --> 01:01:45.507
The cursed tools I use are
imbued with cursed energy

01:01:45.640 --> 01:01:46.941
by someone else.

01:01:47.074 --> 01:01:48.342
It doesn't come from me.

01:01:50.211 --> 01:01:53.013
At least this helped get
me out of that family.

01:01:53.147 --> 01:01:55.082
The food was awful, the
rooms were minuscule,

01:01:55.216 --> 01:01:57.686
and it was crawling
with strange old men.

01:01:57.818 --> 01:02:00.054
The whole experience
totally sucked.

01:02:02.223 --> 01:02:03.958
Don't use my last name.

01:02:04.091 --> 01:02:05.527
Not everyone's like you.

01:02:05.660 --> 01:02:08.329
Most people don't have
resistance to curses.

01:02:08.462 --> 01:02:10.864
Don't ask me about
cursed energy.

01:02:14.569 --> 01:02:17.805
[Yuta] So then why are you
still a jujutsu sorcerer?

01:02:17.938 --> 01:02:20.207
Because I happen to be spiteful.

01:02:21.008 --> 01:02:23.043
I plan on returning
to my family one day

01:02:23.177 --> 01:02:25.112
as a grade-one sorcerer.

01:02:25.246 --> 01:02:28.249
And then I'll obliterate
the Zen'in clan from within.

01:02:28.382 --> 01:02:30.884
I'll show them that you
don't need to see curses

01:02:31.018 --> 01:02:32.486
to be a great sorcerer.

01:02:36.390 --> 01:02:37.458
What is it?

01:02:37.592 --> 01:02:40.361
I was just thinking,
that's so like you.

01:02:41.696 --> 01:02:42.896
I wish,

01:02:44.231 --> 01:02:46.668
I wish I could be just like you.

01:02:46.800 --> 01:02:49.638
You know, strong,
and determined.

01:02:49.770 --> 01:02:52.507
(gentle music)

01:02:56.910 --> 01:02:58.212
Honestly, Maki.

01:02:58.345 --> 01:03:00.481
You're the shame
of the Zen'in clan.

01:03:00.615 --> 01:03:01.949
I wish you were never born.

01:03:02.082 --> 01:03:03.450
Everyone, look.

01:03:03.585 --> 01:03:05.152
Look at Maki.

01:03:06.153 --> 01:03:08.355
You don't want to
turn out like her.

01:03:16.864 --> 01:03:19.634
If there's ever anything I can
help you with, just ask me.

01:03:19.768 --> 01:03:23.370
You know, like, obliterating
your clan or something.

01:03:23.505 --> 01:03:26.307
(Yuta giggles)

01:03:26.907 --> 01:03:28.242
You moron.

01:03:28.375 --> 01:03:30.512
There's no point if I
don't do it by myself.

01:03:31.646 --> 01:03:32.813
I'm going back to my room.

01:03:32.946 --> 01:03:34.516
[Yuta] Okay, later.

01:03:34.649 --> 01:03:37.519
(door whooshes)

01:03:39.119 --> 01:03:41.088
Come on, Maki,
don't be an idiot.

01:03:42.323 --> 01:03:44.958
Don't start believing that
you've really been accepted.

01:03:46.327 --> 01:03:49.496
Emerge from darkness
blacker still.

01:03:49.631 --> 01:03:52.333
Purify that which is impure.

01:03:52.466 --> 01:03:55.503
(veil squelching)

01:03:55.637 --> 01:03:56.504
(Yuta groans)

01:03:56.638 --> 01:03:57.505
(Maki groans)

01:03:57.639 --> 01:03:59.440
(suspenseful music)

01:03:59.574 --> 01:04:02.042
A veil's being drawn
over the school?

01:04:02.176 --> 01:04:03.444
But by who and why?

01:04:04.646 --> 01:04:07.448
(monsters grunting)

01:04:09.651 --> 01:04:11.352
Try to keep the
destruction of buildings

01:04:11.485 --> 01:04:13.320
and the infrastructure
to a minimum.

01:04:13.454 --> 01:04:16.156
There's a chance some civilians
still haven't evacuated.

01:04:16.290 --> 01:04:18.459
If you find any, get
them out of here.

01:04:19.059 --> 01:04:20.562
Are you listening to me, Gojo?

01:04:21.328 --> 01:04:24.599
There's one who may
cause us some trouble.

01:04:25.999 --> 01:04:28.536
That bandaged guy,
I'll take him on.

01:04:29.436 --> 01:04:30.538
Sounds good.

01:04:30.672 --> 01:04:32.540
We'll take on the other
jujutsu sorcerers.

01:04:32.674 --> 01:04:33.907
Just one last reminder.

01:04:34.041 --> 01:04:35.376
Yeah, I know.

01:04:35.510 --> 01:04:37.311
We're only supposed
to be stalling them.

01:04:37.444 --> 01:04:40.013
Let's just take it
easy and have some fun

01:04:40.147 --> 01:04:42.416
until Geto finishes his job.

01:04:42.550 --> 01:04:44.552
What are you doing here?

01:04:44.686 --> 01:04:46.120
Is it a problem that I am?

01:04:46.253 --> 01:04:49.390
I think the real question
is, what are you doing here?

01:04:50.658 --> 01:04:52.092
Sorry about this,

01:04:52.226 --> 01:04:54.562
but I don't have time
to chat with monkeys.

01:04:55.229 --> 01:04:57.565
[Ijichi] Gojo, I have a report.

01:04:59.099 --> 01:05:00.568
What's the matter?

01:05:00.702 --> 01:05:01.902
Oh.

01:05:02.704 --> 01:05:04.204
That guy loves to show off,

01:05:04.338 --> 01:05:06.574
and yet he's not
on the front lines?

01:05:06.708 --> 01:05:08.175
Is he in Kyoto?

01:05:08.308 --> 01:05:11.211
We should have received
some kind of word if he was.

01:05:11.345 --> 01:05:13.515
Just lost in thought, what's up?

01:05:13.648 --> 01:05:15.949
I know this isn't
really the best time,

01:05:16.083 --> 01:05:17.451
but I thought you should know.

01:05:17.585 --> 01:05:19.286
It's about the
investigation into Yuta

01:05:19.420 --> 01:05:21.422
that you requested earlier.

01:05:24.626 --> 01:05:25.492
(Satoru gasps)

01:05:25.627 --> 01:05:26.493
[Satoru] Panda, Toge.

01:05:26.628 --> 01:05:27.762
Hmm?

01:05:27.896 --> 01:05:28.962
What is it?

01:05:29.096 --> 01:05:30.532
- (Panda groaning)
- No questions.

01:05:30.665 --> 01:05:33.635
I'm sending both of you
to Jujutsu High right now.

01:05:33.768 --> 01:05:35.002
Huh?

01:05:35.135 --> 01:05:36.003
[Satoru] Geto is there.

01:05:36.136 --> 01:05:37.237
He has to be.

01:05:37.371 --> 01:05:38.840
I'm absolutely certain of it.

01:05:38.972 --> 01:05:39.841
Probably.

01:05:39.973 --> 01:05:41.141
Well, which is it?

01:05:41.275 --> 01:05:42.744
[Satoru] If my
intuition is right,

01:05:42.877 --> 01:05:44.978
Yuta and Maki might both die.

01:05:45.112 --> 01:05:46.648
(Panda gasps)

01:05:46.781 --> 01:05:48.982
I'll join you after I take
care of that foreign sorcerer.

01:05:49.116 --> 01:05:50.384
Protect the two of them.

01:05:50.518 --> 01:05:52.587
Defend them with your lives.

01:05:54.288 --> 01:05:56.089
- Right.
- [Toge] Salmon.

01:05:56.223 --> 01:05:58.192
(wind whooshes)

01:05:58.325 --> 01:05:59.493
(Suda groans)

01:05:59.627 --> 01:06:01.128
[Suda] No way, they
figured it out?

01:06:01.261 --> 01:06:02.530
[Miguel] This is why I said,

01:06:02.664 --> 01:06:05.098
you should at least
prepare a stand-in.

01:06:05.232 --> 01:06:07.100
Geto didn't wanna
use a bad dummy.

01:06:07.234 --> 01:06:09.470
He said it would
make things worse.

01:06:09.604 --> 01:06:10.605
Mimiko, Nanako.

01:06:11.438 --> 01:06:12.306
What?

01:06:12.574 --> 01:06:13.875
[Suda] We're
stepping up the plan.

01:06:14.007 --> 01:06:15.108
Engage.

01:06:15.242 --> 01:06:16.443
(Nanako giggles)

01:06:18.546 --> 01:06:20.548
I've been waiting for this.

01:06:20.682 --> 01:06:22.684
(suspenseful music)

01:06:22.817 --> 01:06:24.886
Let me introduce myself.

01:06:25.018 --> 01:06:27.789
I'm Miguel, your opponent.

01:06:27.922 --> 01:06:32.627
[Satoru] Sorry, Miguel but
I'm in a hurry right now.

01:06:36.163 --> 01:06:37.030
(wind whooshes)

01:06:37.164 --> 01:06:38.131
A veil's been drawn.

01:06:38.265 --> 01:06:40.033
Satoru's intuition was right.

01:06:40.167 --> 01:06:41.569
I'll break the veil.

01:06:41.703 --> 01:06:43.605
Then we'll take the
shortest most direct route.

01:06:43.738 --> 01:06:44.639
Let's go.

01:06:44.772 --> 01:06:45.974
[Toge] Pollack roe.

01:06:46.106 --> 01:06:47.575
Oh.

01:06:47.709 --> 01:06:48.843
(Suguru giggles)

01:06:48.977 --> 01:06:51.546
Looks like someone made
a hole in the veil.

01:06:51.679 --> 01:06:52.947
(Suguru sighs)

01:06:53.080 --> 01:06:56.083
It seems like these things
never go quite as planned.

01:06:56.216 --> 01:06:58.018
It should take them
about five minutes

01:06:58.151 --> 01:07:00.487
from the point of
entry to get here.

01:07:00.622 --> 01:07:03.791
Should I ignore them, or
should I take care of them?

01:07:04.993 --> 01:07:07.494
It's just so hard to decide.

01:07:08.696 --> 01:07:11.733
(explosion booms)

01:07:12.834 --> 01:07:14.167
Did they break through the walls

01:07:14.301 --> 01:07:16.704
to take the shortest
route to me?

01:07:16.838 --> 01:07:18.472
Not bad.

01:07:18.606 --> 01:07:21.709
(Panda grunts)

01:07:21.843 --> 01:07:22.710
[Panda] Maki.

01:07:23.176 --> 01:07:24.044
- (foot thuds)
- (Panda grunts)

01:07:24.177 --> 01:07:25.379
Focus.

01:07:26.146 --> 01:07:27.447
- (fist thuds)
- (Panda grunts)

01:07:27.582 --> 01:07:30.183
[Panda] This guy can
handle close combat, too?

01:07:31.986 --> 01:07:34.756
(Panda grunts)

01:07:39.894 --> 01:07:42.764
(Panda grunts)

01:07:42.897 --> 01:07:43.698
Oh?

01:07:43.831 --> 01:07:46.734
(Panda grunting)

01:07:52.205 --> 01:07:55.108
(Panda grunting)

01:07:56.076 --> 01:07:57.545
You're very predictable.

01:07:57.679 --> 01:07:59.881
Because I was setting you up.

01:08:00.014 --> 01:08:01.281
(air whooshes)

01:08:01.415 --> 01:08:03.618
[Panda] Drumming Beat.

01:08:07.889 --> 01:08:10.792
(Panda grunting)

01:08:10.925 --> 01:08:13.928
(Geto chuckes)

01:08:14.062 --> 01:08:16.864
(Panda grunting)

01:08:19.199 --> 01:08:20.068
- (stick whooshes)
- (Geto grunts)

01:08:20.200 --> 01:08:22.670
(Panda grunts)

01:08:22.804 --> 01:08:23.504
(Panda groans)

01:08:23.638 --> 01:08:25.073
Boy, that was a close one.

01:08:25.205 --> 01:08:26.874
[Panda] I couldn't agree more.

01:08:29.510 --> 01:08:30.511
Plummet.

01:08:31.746 --> 01:08:34.582
(explosion booms)

01:08:38.886 --> 01:08:40.922
Toge, are you okay?

01:08:41.055 --> 01:08:42.322
Caviar.

01:08:42.456 --> 01:08:44.626
Good, come on,
let's check on Maki.

01:08:47.829 --> 01:08:49.463
Maki, are you okay?

01:08:49.597 --> 01:08:50.263
Maki?

01:08:50.397 --> 01:08:51.666
[Toge] Mustard leaf.

01:08:51.799 --> 01:08:52.667
(Maki groans)

01:08:52.800 --> 01:08:53.668
No.

01:08:53.801 --> 01:08:55.637
No, not yet, don't.

01:08:55.770 --> 01:08:56.638
Huh?

01:08:56.771 --> 01:08:58.271
(Toge groans)

01:08:58.405 --> 01:09:01.341
(ground rumbles)

01:09:05.278 --> 01:09:06.848
(Yuta groans)

01:09:06.981 --> 01:09:08.215
Another earthquake?

01:09:08.348 --> 01:09:10.350
I wonder what's
going on down there.

01:09:12.987 --> 01:09:13.788
Wonderful.

01:09:13.921 --> 01:09:15.590
Simply wonderful.

01:09:15.723 --> 01:09:18.626
I'm so incredibly
touched right now.

01:09:18.760 --> 01:09:21.663
You all raced down here
to save Yuta Okkotsu.

01:09:21.796 --> 01:09:25.967
Jujutsu sorcerers sacrificing
themselves for a colleague.

01:09:26.100 --> 01:09:27.300
Such affection.

01:09:27.434 --> 01:09:28.603
Such admiration.

01:09:28.736 --> 01:09:30.505
This is the world I long for.

01:09:30.638 --> 01:09:33.240
All here right before my eyes.

01:09:33.373 --> 01:09:36.577
(suspenseful music)

01:09:40.882 --> 01:09:41.883
Maki, no.

01:09:42.984 --> 01:09:44.418
To be honest with you.

01:09:44.552 --> 01:09:47.789
I wanted you to live
too, Yuta, I really did.

01:09:47.922 --> 01:09:51.759
But this battle is for the
future of the jujutsu world.

01:09:51.893 --> 01:09:52.894
Panda.

01:09:54.194 --> 01:09:55.563
[Toge] Yuta.

01:09:57.765 --> 01:09:58.766
[Yuta] Toge.

01:10:00.300 --> 01:10:02.837
Run away.

01:10:05.405 --> 01:10:07.909
(Yuta grunts)

01:10:09.342 --> 01:10:10.912
Come out, Rika.

01:10:12.647 --> 01:10:15.850
(suspenseful music)

01:10:17.051 --> 01:10:18.886
I'm going to kill you.

01:10:19.020 --> 01:10:20.420
Not before you die.

01:10:21.321 --> 01:10:24.525
(suspenseful music)

01:10:33.333 --> 01:10:34.535
(monster growling)

01:10:34.669 --> 01:10:36.571
Quantity before quality.

01:10:36.704 --> 01:10:39.774
What's your next
move Queen of Curses?

01:10:39.907 --> 01:10:42.810
(monster growling)

01:10:47.181 --> 01:10:52.053
- (monsters squelching)
- (monsters growling)

01:10:52.186 --> 01:10:53.054
(Rika growls)

01:10:53.187 --> 01:10:56.057
(explosion booms)

01:10:56.190 --> 01:10:57.592
[Yuta] Good job, Rika.

01:11:01.461 --> 01:11:04.866
These three are horribly
wounded, especially Maki.

01:11:04.999 --> 01:11:06.501
(Maki groans)

01:11:06.634 --> 01:11:08.268
I won't let you die.

01:11:10.772 --> 01:11:14.575
(Maki breathes heavily)

01:11:16.544 --> 01:11:18.980
Not fair, not fair, not fair.

01:11:19.113 --> 01:11:20.081
It's always you.

01:11:20.214 --> 01:11:21.983
It was always you.

01:11:22.116 --> 01:11:23.251
What are you doing, Rika?

01:11:23.383 --> 01:11:24.484
Huh?

01:11:24.619 --> 01:11:26.087
That's the woman
who saved my life.

01:11:26.220 --> 01:11:28.723
Handle her with more care
than you would a butterfly

01:11:28.856 --> 01:11:29.857
or a flower.

01:11:31.125 --> 01:11:33.460
(Rika groans)

01:11:33.594 --> 01:11:34.929
I'm sorry, Yuta.

01:11:35.062 --> 01:11:36.097
I'm sorry.

01:11:36.230 --> 01:11:37.965
Please don't be mad.

01:11:38.099 --> 01:11:39.299
I'm not mad at you.

01:11:39.432 --> 01:11:41.102
Please, I don't
want you to hate me.

01:11:41.235 --> 01:11:42.970
I could never hate you.

01:11:44.739 --> 01:11:47.008
Our enemy is that man there.

01:11:47.141 --> 01:11:49.476
[Rika] Yuta, do you hate him?

01:11:49.610 --> 01:11:51.546
[Yuta] Yes, I loathe him.

01:11:53.080 --> 01:11:55.116
Then I will hate him, too.

01:11:55.249 --> 01:11:57.051
Welcome back.

01:11:58.318 --> 01:12:00.221
Why did you stop attacking?

01:12:00.353 --> 01:12:01.656
Healing with cursed energy

01:12:01.789 --> 01:12:04.892
requires an advanced
reverse cursed technique.

01:12:05.026 --> 01:12:06.194
It was more advantageous

01:12:06.326 --> 01:12:08.996
to let you divide your
attention over there.

01:12:09.130 --> 01:12:11.364
But now that you're back,

01:12:11.498 --> 01:12:13.935
shall we pick up
where we left off?

01:12:14.068 --> 01:12:15.468
(monsters hissing)

01:12:15.603 --> 01:12:16.938
Rika, give it to me.

01:12:20.775 --> 01:12:22.710
[Suguru] Snake Eyes and Fangs?

01:12:22.844 --> 01:12:26.981
Those are the cursed
seals of the Inumaki clan.

01:12:27.648 --> 01:12:31.219
(suspenseful music)

01:12:31.351 --> 01:12:34.555
(monsters growling)

01:12:35.455 --> 01:12:36.657
Die.

01:12:40.161 --> 01:12:42.997
(explosion booms)

01:12:44.065 --> 01:12:45.099
How wonderful.

01:12:46.334 --> 01:12:48.135
Cursed speech is a powerful
technique passed down

01:12:48.269 --> 01:12:51.438
in the Inumaki clan, yet
this young man pulled it off

01:12:51.572 --> 01:12:54.075
with less than a year
of studying jujutsu.

01:12:54.208 --> 01:12:55.843
That really is hard to use.

01:12:55.977 --> 01:12:58.880
The cursed energy scatters,
and it's hard to focus at.

01:12:59.580 --> 01:13:00.848
Inumaki's incredible.

01:13:02.016 --> 01:13:03.117
I see now.

01:13:03.251 --> 01:13:05.853
Rika Orimoto's true
form, it's ever-changing.

01:13:05.987 --> 01:13:08.356
She's a bastion
of cursed energy.

01:13:08.488 --> 01:13:09.891
It's true.

01:13:10.024 --> 01:13:12.927
All my friend's are
so amazing and strong.

01:13:13.060 --> 01:13:14.095
And you Rika.

01:13:14.228 --> 01:13:15.428
You are, too.

01:13:15.563 --> 01:13:18.065
Sorry, but I need
her more than you do.

01:13:19.834 --> 01:13:21.736
[Yuta] I'll beat you to a pulp.

01:13:25.405 --> 01:13:26.641
(explosion booms)

01:13:26.774 --> 01:13:31.979
- (man grunting)
- (fist thudding)

01:13:32.380 --> 01:13:33.948
(monster growls)

01:13:34.081 --> 01:13:36.918
(man grunting)

01:13:37.051 --> 01:13:39.754
(monster groans)

01:13:43.090 --> 01:13:44.025
(man grunting)

01:13:44.158 --> 01:13:47.561
(monster blood splashes)

01:13:50.631 --> 01:13:52.066
Whoo.

01:13:52.199 --> 01:13:53.267
Nanami's here.

01:13:53.401 --> 01:13:54.769
Good, he'll get a
chance to see me.

01:13:54.902 --> 01:13:56.771
This is my shot to
really impress him.

01:13:56.904 --> 01:13:58.139
- Huh?
- Will you shut up?

01:13:58.272 --> 01:14:00.641
Quit bubling about
yourself and fight.

01:14:00.775 --> 01:14:01.976
There's still a lot more coming.

01:14:02.109 --> 01:14:04.645
- (monster growls)
- (Kusakabe grunts)

01:14:04.779 --> 01:14:06.781
Man, what a pain.

01:14:08.649 --> 01:14:10.351
(Mei giggles)

01:14:10.483 --> 01:14:13.521
(blade whooshing)

01:14:16.090 --> 01:14:17.024
(Mei giggles)

01:14:17.158 --> 01:14:20.194
(blade whooshing)

01:14:21.996 --> 01:14:24.231
(Mei grunts)

01:14:27.234 --> 01:14:28.102
(blade clanging)

01:14:28.235 --> 01:14:29.937
That makes it 50 kills.

01:14:30.071 --> 01:14:32.139
I've passed the numbers
needed for the incentive.

01:14:32.273 --> 01:14:34.175
It's time to work
a little bit harder

01:14:34.308 --> 01:14:37.545
and then I'll be taking
home that full bonus pay.

01:14:41.749 --> 01:14:43.551
Oh, my, how old are you two?

01:14:43.684 --> 01:14:44.919
[Nanako] 15.

01:14:45.052 --> 01:14:46.988
You're still just children.

01:14:47.121 --> 01:14:49.290
It's not too late
for you to turn back.

01:14:50.024 --> 01:14:51.459
You don't even
know the difference

01:14:51.592 --> 01:14:53.527
between right and wrong yet.

01:14:53.661 --> 01:14:54.962
You're annoying.

01:14:55.096 --> 01:14:57.531
Mimiko, doesn't he
totally piss you off?

01:14:57.665 --> 01:14:59.567
Shall we hang him, Nanako?

01:14:59.700 --> 01:15:00.668
You're oblivious.

01:15:00.801 --> 01:15:02.703
You have no idea.

01:15:02.837 --> 01:15:05.006
You don't know how jujutsu
sorcerers are treated

01:15:05.139 --> 01:15:07.675
when they grow up out
in the damn sticks,

01:15:07.808 --> 01:15:09.710
in places not even on maps.

01:15:10.644 --> 01:15:12.747
Right and wrong?
(Nanako scoffs)

01:15:12.880 --> 01:15:16.183
All of you just go ahead
and enjoy that stuff.

01:15:16.317 --> 01:15:19.653
The way Mr. Geto puts
it, black is white,

01:15:19.787 --> 01:15:21.989
and white is black, too.

01:15:24.992 --> 01:15:26.727
When Mr. Geto found us,

01:15:26.861 --> 01:15:30.765
he shared his vision for
a wonderful new world.

01:15:31.732 --> 01:15:34.335
And anyone who gets in
his way, we'll hang.

01:15:34.468 --> 01:15:35.504
(explosion booms)

01:15:35.636 --> 01:15:39.140
(Nanako and Mimiko groans)

01:15:39.273 --> 01:15:40.141
Miguel?

01:15:40.274 --> 01:15:41.375
What are you doing here?

01:15:41.510 --> 01:15:43.210
Take a look and figure it out.

01:15:43.344 --> 01:15:45.246
[Satoru] You're a tenacious one.

01:15:45.913 --> 01:15:48.783
(rope whooshes)

01:15:49.917 --> 01:15:53.687
That rope, it has an
unusual curse woven into it.

01:15:53.821 --> 01:15:55.756
It's disrupting my techniques.

01:15:56.757 --> 01:15:58.993
[Miguel] I barely have
half of my rope left.

01:15:59.126 --> 01:16:01.562
How many decades do you
think it took the sorcerers

01:16:01.695 --> 01:16:06.233
in my country to weave this
rope imbued with cursed energy?

01:16:06.367 --> 01:16:07.536
Like I care.

01:16:07.668 --> 01:16:09.538
I can outmatch it
in about one second.

01:16:09.670 --> 01:16:11.806
(monster laughing)

01:16:11.939 --> 01:16:13.140
You're in the way.

01:16:14.375 --> 01:16:16.277
(monster groans)

01:16:16.410 --> 01:16:18.279
(explosion booms)

01:16:18.412 --> 01:16:19.413
(Mimiko and Nanako groans)

01:16:19.548 --> 01:16:20.748
[Ijichi] Oh, no,
this isn't good.

01:16:20.881 --> 01:16:22.283
Gojo's snapped.

01:16:22.416 --> 01:16:24.585
[Miguel] So, this is the
limitless jujutsu technique

01:16:24.718 --> 01:16:26.020
that Geto mentioned.

01:16:26.153 --> 01:16:28.222
It interferes on
an atomic level,

01:16:28.355 --> 01:16:29.924
controlling space and time

01:16:30.057 --> 01:16:33.160
with precise manipulation
of cursed energy.

01:16:33.294 --> 01:16:36.831
And what makes it all possible
is the power of his eyes.

01:16:36.964 --> 01:16:40.502
I have just 12 more minutes
until my quota runs out.

01:16:40.634 --> 01:16:42.369
I'll keep fight for my life.

01:16:43.704 --> 01:16:45.473
- (rope whooshes)
- (Miguel grunts)

01:16:45.606 --> 01:16:47.741
(object crashes)

01:16:47.875 --> 01:16:53.080
- (Miguel grunting)
- (rope whooshing)

01:16:56.817 --> 01:16:59.687
(Miguel grunts)

01:17:01.789 --> 01:17:05.092
(electricity buzzes)

01:17:05.759 --> 01:17:07.261
(Satoru grunts)

01:17:07.394 --> 01:17:10.297
(explosion booms)

01:17:10.431 --> 01:17:13.300
(monster growls)

01:17:13.434 --> 01:17:16.605
(monster groaning)

01:17:16.737 --> 01:17:17.606
Whoa.

01:17:17.738 --> 01:17:19.140
(ground rumbles)

01:17:19.273 --> 01:17:22.109
(Miguel groaning)

01:17:23.777 --> 01:17:26.548
(Miguel grunting)

01:17:26.680 --> 01:17:29.350
(Miguel groans)

01:17:34.288 --> 01:17:39.293
- (Miguel grunting)
- (fists thudding)

01:17:46.033 --> 01:17:49.136
(monster growling)

01:17:49.837 --> 01:17:52.273
That last round was dangerous.

01:17:52.406 --> 01:17:53.807
I need to be more focus.

01:17:53.941 --> 01:17:55.075
10 more minutes.

01:17:55.209 --> 01:17:57.144
Time to give
everything I've got.

01:17:57.278 --> 01:18:00.314
If I die tonight, I'm
cursing you, Geto.

01:18:00.447 --> 01:18:03.284
(people groaning)

01:18:04.485 --> 01:18:06.387
[Akari] Shoko, this
one needs your help.

01:18:06.521 --> 01:18:08.756
Just set him down and
I'll be there soon.

01:18:08.889 --> 01:18:10.491
[Akari] Right.
Look at this.

01:18:10.625 --> 01:18:11.825
What were you all doing?

01:18:11.959 --> 01:18:13.260
You're gonna be okay.

01:18:13.394 --> 01:18:16.330
Shoko's gonna fix you
right up, all right?

01:18:17.632 --> 01:18:18.899
We're counting on you.

01:18:20.968 --> 01:18:22.236
(Shoko scoffs)

01:18:22.369 --> 01:18:25.706
You really forced a heap
of trouble on us, Geto.

01:18:28.242 --> 01:18:30.744
It's the first time you've
experiencing violent emotions

01:18:30.878 --> 01:18:33.080
as cursed energy fills
your body, isn't it?

01:18:33.214 --> 01:18:36.784
That heightening of physical
prowess, of omnipotence.

01:18:36.917 --> 01:18:39.787
Your senses become
sharper and sharper.

01:18:39.920 --> 01:18:42.856
The riff-raff are no
longer a match for you.

01:18:42.990 --> 01:18:45.226
So, I'll have to
crush you myself.

01:18:46.661 --> 01:18:48.429
Follow my lead, Rika.

01:18:49.230 --> 01:18:52.399
Mankind stands at the
top of the food chain,

01:18:52.534 --> 01:18:54.969
yet they imagined the
existence of higher beings

01:18:55.102 --> 01:18:56.370
and called them gods.

01:18:56.504 --> 01:18:59.139
Don't you find that
awfully strange?

01:18:59.273 --> 01:19:03.277
Especially since jujutsu
sorcerers exist without belief.

01:19:06.514 --> 01:19:09.216
(Rika grunts)

01:19:10.484 --> 01:19:11.385
(Yuta grunts)

01:19:11.519 --> 01:19:14.455
(metal clanging)

01:19:16.691 --> 01:19:19.393
(Rika grunts)

01:19:24.865 --> 01:19:25.899
(Yuta grunts)

01:19:26.033 --> 01:19:28.269
(Rika grunts)

01:19:28.402 --> 01:19:30.371
(metal clanging)

01:19:30.505 --> 01:19:33.173
(Yuta grunting)

01:19:36.310 --> 01:19:39.079
(metal clanging)

01:19:41.448 --> 01:19:43.350
(Geto giggles)

01:19:43.484 --> 01:19:46.420
(metal clanging)

01:19:47.087 --> 01:19:48.822
(Rika grunts)

01:19:48.956 --> 01:19:51.925
(Yuta grunting)

01:19:55.296 --> 01:19:57.131
In the end, all those monkeys

01:19:57.264 --> 01:19:59.933
just want to avert their
eyes from the existence

01:20:00.067 --> 01:20:01.268
of those better than them.

01:20:01.402 --> 01:20:03.170
Are you saying you
wanna be a god?

01:20:03.304 --> 01:20:05.806
That's something
a child would say.

01:20:05.939 --> 01:20:08.275
You're missing the
point, Okkotsu.

01:20:10.612 --> 01:20:13.380
(Rika grunts)

01:20:13.515 --> 01:20:14.381
(monster squelching)

01:20:14.516 --> 01:20:17.017
(Yuta grunts)

01:20:19.654 --> 01:20:22.423
(ground rumbles)

01:20:24.425 --> 01:20:27.061
What I long for isn't any
kind of enlightenment.

01:20:27.194 --> 01:20:28.763
It's a chosen people.

01:20:28.896 --> 01:20:31.332
There are times when the strong
are completely overwhelmed

01:20:31.465 --> 01:20:34.536
by the weak, due to their
strength in sheer numbers.

01:20:34.669 --> 01:20:37.137
And the audacity of
those weak monkeys,

01:20:37.271 --> 01:20:39.173
that they think they
can defeat the strong,

01:20:39.306 --> 01:20:41.375
makes me so sick I could vomit.

01:20:42.610 --> 01:20:44.478
Yuta, are you okay?

01:20:44.612 --> 01:20:45.979
I'm all right, Rika.

01:20:46.113 --> 01:20:47.515
I'm used to it now.

01:20:47.649 --> 01:20:49.818
Are we done debating philosophy?

01:20:49.950 --> 01:20:53.153
(suspenseful music)

01:20:59.661 --> 01:21:01.563
(air whooshing)

01:21:01.696 --> 01:21:03.430
He's even faster now.

01:21:03.565 --> 01:21:04.431
(nunchaku whooshes)

01:21:04.566 --> 01:21:07.167
(air whooshes)

01:21:09.671 --> 01:21:10.538
(blade whooshes)

01:21:10.672 --> 01:21:11.639
(blade crashing)

01:21:11.773 --> 01:21:13.273
You shouldn't have done that.

01:21:13.407 --> 01:21:15.510
When you imbue a curse
like that too abruptly,

01:21:15.643 --> 01:21:17.077
the vessel won't last.

01:21:17.211 --> 01:21:20.782
Didn't Satoru teach you to
imbue curses bit by bit.

01:21:20.914 --> 01:21:21.982
(Geto groans)

01:21:22.116 --> 01:21:23.417
- (fist thuds)
- (Geto grunts)

01:21:23.551 --> 01:21:26.353
(upbeat music)

01:21:34.027 --> 01:21:35.697
The kid's not bad.

01:21:35.830 --> 01:21:37.665
What are you talking about?

01:21:37.799 --> 01:21:40.934
I don't know about any sorcerers
outside of this school,

01:21:41.068 --> 01:21:43.705
so I don't know if
you're right or wrong.

01:21:43.838 --> 01:21:45.573
But I do know one thing.

01:21:45.707 --> 01:21:48.510
I know that in order to
remain here with my friends

01:21:48.643 --> 01:21:51.880
and in order to believe it's
okay that I'm still alive.

01:21:52.012 --> 01:21:53.981
I know what I have to do.

01:21:55.583 --> 01:21:57.151
I have to do it.

01:21:57.284 --> 01:21:59.654
I have no choice
but to kill you.

01:21:59.920 --> 01:22:01.790
You're a little egotistical.

01:22:01.922 --> 01:22:04.291
Nonetheless, just keep it up.

01:22:04.425 --> 01:22:06.260
Those daily self-affirmations.

01:22:06.393 --> 01:22:09.496
There's nothing more
important in life.

01:22:09.631 --> 01:22:11.064
Unfortunately, though,

01:22:11.198 --> 01:22:14.301
I'm going to use my full
force to kill you now.

01:22:14.435 --> 01:22:16.604
No more time for compromise.

01:22:16.738 --> 01:22:19.607
Are you aware, there
are only four people

01:22:19.741 --> 01:22:21.375
who are special-grade?

01:22:21.509 --> 01:22:24.077
Among curses, there are 16.

01:22:24.211 --> 01:22:26.280
Let me introduce
you to one of them.

01:22:26.413 --> 01:22:29.183
Special-grade
potential apparition,

01:22:29.950 --> 01:22:32.352
Incarnate, Tamamo-no-mae.

01:22:33.086 --> 01:22:34.421
On top of that,

01:22:34.556 --> 01:22:39.159
I'll combine the 4,461
curses I possess into one

01:22:39.293 --> 01:22:40.728
and strike you with it.

01:22:43.497 --> 01:22:47.669
Cursed Spirit
Manipulation, Supreme Art.

01:22:47.802 --> 01:22:51.539
(suspenseful music)

01:22:51.673 --> 01:22:52.674
Maelstrom.

01:22:55.810 --> 01:22:57.879
(monster growls)

01:22:58.011 --> 01:23:00.582
(man grunting)

01:23:05.620 --> 01:23:06.688
(blood splashes)

01:23:06.821 --> 01:23:09.223
(man groans)

01:23:11.759 --> 01:23:14.596
(monster giggles)

01:23:22.169 --> 01:23:23.671
(woman groans)

01:23:23.805 --> 01:23:24.706
Mr. Nanami.

01:23:26.875 --> 01:23:28.576
Let me take care of this.

01:23:28.710 --> 01:23:31.513
(upbeat music)

01:23:32.647 --> 01:23:33.815
(wind whooshes)

01:23:33.948 --> 01:23:37.017
(monster growls)

01:23:37.150 --> 01:23:39.988
(monster groans)

01:23:40.120 --> 01:23:43.023
- (monster groaning)
- (blades whooshes)

01:23:43.156 --> 01:23:44.726
(monster groans)

01:23:44.859 --> 01:23:47.529
(glass crashes)

01:23:53.066 --> 01:23:55.637
(Nanami grunts)

01:24:00.407 --> 01:24:01.576
(Nanami grunts)

01:24:01.709 --> 01:24:03.878
(monster groans)

01:24:04.012 --> 01:24:07.281
(monster squelching)

01:24:10.752 --> 01:24:13.621
(air whooshing)

01:24:16.991 --> 01:24:20.294
(explosion booms)

01:24:20.427 --> 01:24:22.730
New Shadow Style Simple Domain.

01:24:22.864 --> 01:24:23.865
Quick Draw.

01:24:23.998 --> 01:24:26.034
(monster squelching)

01:24:26.166 --> 01:24:27.735
(Miwa sighs)

01:24:27.869 --> 01:24:29.771
(fire whooshes)

01:24:29.904 --> 01:24:30.905
Huh?

01:24:31.739 --> 01:24:34.308
[Mechamaru] Don't let
your guard down, Miwa.

01:24:35.810 --> 01:24:36.778
Mechamaru, look out.

01:24:36.911 --> 01:24:39.246
(gun fires)

01:24:40.949 --> 01:24:42.650
You better look out, too.

01:24:43.585 --> 01:24:46.219
[Kamo] Everyone, make
sure you stay alert.

01:24:47.454 --> 01:24:50.490
Kamo, I see seven cursed
spirits heading your way.

01:24:50.625 --> 01:24:52.794
[Kamo] Roger that,
where did Todo go?

01:24:52.927 --> 01:24:54.662
(explosion booms)

01:24:54.796 --> 01:24:59.166
[Momo] Oh, I think you'll
see him soon enough.

01:25:00.034 --> 01:25:02.737
(Todo grunts)

01:25:03.771 --> 01:25:04.839
(Todo chuckles)

01:25:04.973 --> 01:25:07.240
Where have you been
all this time, Todo?

01:25:08.776 --> 01:25:09.644
(ground rumbles)

01:25:09.777 --> 01:25:11.012
(monster growling)

01:25:11.144 --> 01:25:12.747
(Kamo groans) I've never seen
cursed energy like that.

01:25:14.949 --> 01:25:16.249
That one's real dangerous, Todo.

01:25:16.383 --> 01:25:17.484
Don't rush in on your own.

01:25:17.619 --> 01:25:18.920
- Wait for back.
- Sorry,

01:25:19.053 --> 01:25:20.454
but the talk show's
live Christmas special

01:25:20.588 --> 01:25:22.255
is gonna be starting at eight.

01:25:22.389 --> 01:25:24.759
And it'll will be
hosting Takada.

01:25:25.927 --> 01:25:29.530
Let's stop wasting our time
and get this fight over with.

01:25:29.664 --> 01:25:30.665
Todo.

01:25:30.798 --> 01:25:31.966
[Momo] Kamo.

01:25:32.100 --> 01:25:34.167
Another 10 or more cursed
spirits are approaching

01:25:34.301 --> 01:25:35.803
from six o'clock.

01:25:35.937 --> 01:25:36.871
(Kamo groans)

01:25:37.005 --> 01:25:38.606
Everyone, prepare to intercept.

01:25:40.074 --> 01:25:40.942
(Mai scoffs)

01:25:41.075 --> 01:25:42.242
These curses never end.

01:25:42.376 --> 01:25:44.211
When is this finally
going to be over?

01:25:47.849 --> 01:25:50.317
Okkotsu, I'm so happy.

01:25:50.450 --> 01:25:52.754
My timing was perfect
because I came to kill you

01:25:52.887 --> 01:25:56.791
before you could fully
unleash Rika Orimoto.

01:26:03.765 --> 01:26:06.501
[Rika] It's a promise
that when we grow up,

01:26:06.634 --> 01:26:09.369
we're going to get
married to each other.

01:26:09.504 --> 01:26:14.709
[Yuta] Okay, we'll be
together forever and ever.

01:26:16.044 --> 01:26:17.310
All the time.

01:26:23.985 --> 01:26:24.852
Rika.

01:26:24.986 --> 01:26:26.319
[Rika] Yes, Yuta?

01:26:26.453 --> 01:26:29.157
Thank you for always
protecting me.

01:26:29.289 --> 01:26:31.693
Thank you for falling
in love with me.

01:26:32.827 --> 01:26:35.963
Just one last time,
please, lend me your power.

01:26:38.166 --> 01:26:40.333
I have to stop him.

01:26:40.467 --> 01:26:42.937
I won't need anything
else from you after that.

01:26:44.038 --> 01:26:47.875
I'll give you my future,
my heart, my body.

01:26:48.009 --> 01:26:49.677
I'll give you everything.

01:26:50.745 --> 01:26:54.849
From now on, we'll truly
be together forever.

01:26:56.884 --> 01:26:59.352
I love you, Rika.

01:27:01.321 --> 01:27:02.890
Let's die together.

01:27:07.995 --> 01:27:10.865
(Rika grunting)

01:27:12.365 --> 01:27:13.668
Yuta.

01:27:13.801 --> 01:27:14.802
Yuta.

01:27:15.335 --> 01:27:18.072
I love you, I love you.

01:27:18.206 --> 01:27:20.541
[Suguru] Is he offering
himself as a sacrifice

01:27:20.675 --> 01:27:23.310
to release the limit
on her cursed energy?

01:27:23.443 --> 01:27:24.746
(Geto grunts)

01:27:24.879 --> 01:27:27.148
I never realized you
were such a womanizer.

01:27:27.280 --> 01:27:28.649
Don't be rude.

01:27:30.184 --> 01:27:31.652
Our love is pure.

01:27:32.419 --> 01:27:33.988
Fine, you fight for love.

01:27:34.122 --> 01:27:36.423
I'll fight to win.

01:28:21.135 --> 01:28:22.003
(Geto giggles)

01:28:22.136 --> 01:28:23.504
It's wonderful.

01:28:24.739 --> 01:28:27.608
The whole thing is
absolutely wonderful.

01:28:27.742 --> 01:28:30.845
It truly is the power
to change the world.

01:28:30.978 --> 01:28:33.480
If I had Rika, there
would be no need

01:28:33.614 --> 01:28:36.017
to sneak around
gathering curses.

01:28:36.818 --> 01:28:41.321
Next time, I'll get my
hands on her for sure.

01:28:46.661 --> 01:28:50.631
You're late again
as usual, Satoru.

01:28:51.933 --> 01:28:54.702
To think you'd be the
one here at my end.

01:28:54.836 --> 01:28:57.104
Are you going to make
sure my family is safe?

01:28:57.238 --> 01:29:00.541
Every last one of them
managed to escape to safety.

01:29:00.675 --> 01:29:03.476
The ones in Kyoto, they
were under your command?

01:29:04.212 --> 01:29:05.680
Yes, they all were.

01:29:05.813 --> 01:29:09.183
I'm a kind person
unlike you, Satoru.

01:29:10.417 --> 01:29:13.054
You sent those two assuming
that I'd defeat them,

01:29:13.187 --> 01:29:14.055
didn't you?

01:29:14.188 --> 01:29:16.257
To set Okkotsu off.

01:29:16.389 --> 01:29:18.491
I trusted you'd be yourself.

01:29:18.626 --> 01:29:20.728
Trusted that a man
as principled as you

01:29:20.862 --> 01:29:24.265
wouldn't kill off young
sorcerers without a reason.

01:29:24.397 --> 01:29:25.333
(Geto chuckles)

01:29:25.465 --> 01:29:27.001
You wanna talk about trust?

01:29:30.905 --> 01:29:33.774
I didn't think I had
any of that left in me,

01:29:33.908 --> 01:29:36.010
after everything
I've been through.

01:29:38.813 --> 01:29:40.615
Return this for me, will you?

01:29:42.917 --> 01:29:46.120
[Satoru] Was the elementary
school your doing, too?

01:29:46.254 --> 01:29:47.521
It was.

01:29:47.655 --> 01:29:49.123
I can't believe you.

01:29:51.025 --> 01:29:53.961
Tell me, do you
have any last words?

01:29:55.029 --> 01:29:59.867
No matter what anyone tells
you, I hate those monkeys.

01:30:01.335 --> 01:30:03.738
But I never held any hatred

01:30:03.871 --> 01:30:06.073
for those in
Jujutsu High School.

01:30:07.041 --> 01:30:09.844
I just couldn't wear
a heartfelt smile

01:30:09.977 --> 01:30:11.712
while living in this world.

01:30:14.515 --> 01:30:16.017
Suguru.

01:30:16.150 --> 01:30:18.920
(dramatic music)

01:30:34.434 --> 01:30:35.736
(Geto chuckles)

01:30:35.870 --> 01:30:38.906
The least you could do is
hit me with some curses.

01:30:53.254 --> 01:30:54.454
(slicing)

01:30:56.791 --> 01:30:59.760
- [Maki] Hey, wake up.
- [Panda] Yuta, Yuta.

01:31:01.329 --> 01:31:03.331
Hey, Yuta, are you okay?

01:31:03.463 --> 01:31:04.365
[Toge] Mustard leaf.

01:31:04.497 --> 01:31:07.034
Come on and wake up, Yuta.

01:31:07.668 --> 01:31:08.970
(Yuta groans)

01:31:09.103 --> 01:31:10.237
Good, he's awake.

01:31:11.238 --> 01:31:13.140
(Yuta groans)

01:31:13.274 --> 01:31:14.041
You're all here.

01:31:14.175 --> 01:31:16.043
Maki, your okay?

01:31:16.177 --> 01:31:17.178
Inumaki.

01:31:17.311 --> 01:31:19.981
Whoa, Panda, your
arm hasn't healed.

01:31:20.114 --> 01:31:21.349
Chill out, dude.

01:31:21.481 --> 01:31:23.818
We're all doing way better
than you are right now.

01:31:23.951 --> 01:31:26.153
Unlike these other two losers,

01:31:26.287 --> 01:31:27.955
my arm can be fixed later.

01:31:28.089 --> 01:31:30.558
By the way, thanks
for saving us, Yuta.

01:31:30.691 --> 01:31:31.859
[Toge] Salmon.

01:31:32.360 --> 01:31:33.928
(Yuta groans)

01:31:34.061 --> 01:31:35.062
[Rika] Yuta.

01:31:41.535 --> 01:31:42.636
[Panda] Hmm?

01:31:42.770 --> 01:31:44.739
Sorry about that, Rika.

01:31:44.872 --> 01:31:46.474
I didn't mean to
keep you waiting.

01:31:46.607 --> 01:31:48.009
[Panda] What's the matter?

01:31:48.142 --> 01:31:49.143
Yuta?

01:31:49.977 --> 01:31:54.215
Well, you see, in exchange
for borrowing her power,

01:31:54.348 --> 01:31:57.551
I kind of promised to go and
live with Rika from now on.

01:31:57.685 --> 01:31:58.853
[Maki] What?
Are you crazy?

01:31:58.986 --> 01:32:00.588
Don't you know that means dying?

01:32:00.721 --> 01:32:02.089
What were you
thinking, you idiot?

01:32:02.223 --> 01:32:05.026
Well, I was caught off
in the moment, I guess.

01:32:05.159 --> 01:32:06.093
I don't know.

01:32:06.227 --> 01:32:07.328
Huh?

01:32:07.461 --> 01:32:08.662
Huh?

01:32:09.463 --> 01:32:10.564
[Yuta] Rika?

01:32:10.698 --> 01:32:12.199
(Satoru claps)

01:32:12.333 --> 01:32:13.601
Congratulations.

01:32:13.734 --> 01:32:15.669
You managed to break the curse.

01:32:15.803 --> 01:32:17.138
[All] Who're you?

01:32:17.271 --> 01:32:19.940
I'm your good-looking
teacher, Satoru Gojo.

01:32:20.741 --> 01:32:22.343
I thought the
theory Yuta came up

01:32:22.476 --> 01:32:23.878
with sounded interesting.

01:32:24.011 --> 01:32:27.148
So, I requested an investigation
into their families.

01:32:27.281 --> 01:32:28.883
The investigation
about Rika's family

01:32:29.016 --> 01:32:30.918
came to me long time ago,

01:32:31.052 --> 01:32:34.523
but Yuta's history was
full of holes at best.

01:32:34.655 --> 01:32:37.058
That's when it
finally came to light.

01:32:38.025 --> 01:32:40.761
You're the descendant
of Sugawara Michizane,

01:32:40.895 --> 01:32:43.197
which makes us super
distant relatives.

01:32:43.330 --> 01:32:44.198
[Panda And Maki] Suga?

01:32:44.331 --> 01:32:45.566
Who's Suga?

01:32:45.699 --> 01:32:47.468
One of Japan's three
great apparitions.

01:32:47.601 --> 01:32:49.370
He was a super bigshot sorcerer.

01:32:49.504 --> 01:32:50.704
[Toge] Tuna.

01:32:50.838 --> 01:32:52.573
You were right the
whole time, Yuta.

01:32:52.706 --> 01:32:54.909
Rika didn't place
a curse on you.

01:32:55.042 --> 01:32:57.812
You placed a curse on Rika.

01:33:02.517 --> 01:33:04.151
[Yuta] Rika, what do I do?

01:33:04.285 --> 01:33:05.419
Is she going to die?

01:33:05.554 --> 01:33:06.887
I have to save her.

01:33:07.021 --> 01:33:10.791
Don't die, don't die,
don't die, don't die.

01:33:12.626 --> 01:33:14.028
That's right.

01:33:14.161 --> 01:33:18.567
At the time, I refused
to accept Rika's death.

01:33:18.699 --> 01:33:22.236
Now the one who placed the
curse has canceled the bond.

01:33:23.370 --> 01:33:24.772
As long as the person

01:33:24.905 --> 01:33:27.308
who was cursed doesn't seek
retribution against you,

01:33:27.441 --> 01:33:29.310
the curse is fully broken.

01:33:29.443 --> 01:33:30.811
Of course, that much was obvious

01:33:30.945 --> 01:33:33.047
after seeing her in that form.

01:33:33.180 --> 01:33:35.382
(Yuta cries)

01:33:36.183 --> 01:33:38.219
It was all my fault, wasn't it?

01:33:39.086 --> 01:33:40.955
I turned you into that form.

01:33:42.223 --> 01:33:46.227
I hurt all those people and I
nearly caused everyone to die

01:33:46.360 --> 01:33:48.863
when Geto came after me.

01:33:48.996 --> 01:33:51.765
It's all, it's all my fault.

01:33:52.567 --> 01:33:55.302
(Yuta cries)

01:33:55.436 --> 01:34:00.174
Yuta, thank you for
giving me more time,

01:34:00.307 --> 01:34:03.010
and letting me
stay by your side.

01:34:03.144 --> 01:34:05.246
During the six
years I was cursed,

01:34:05.379 --> 01:34:08.115
I've been happier than
I ever was before.

01:34:09.917 --> 01:34:12.319
(Yuta cries)

01:34:21.962 --> 01:34:23.898
Bye, Yuta, take care.

01:34:27.101 --> 01:34:31.138
And don't cross to my
side anytime soon, okay?

01:34:31.939 --> 01:34:33.340
See you later.

01:34:33.474 --> 01:34:36.076
(gentle music)

01:35:09.210 --> 01:35:11.011
It's a bit late to tell you,

01:35:11.145 --> 01:35:13.948
but you weren't at fault
for the incident with Geto.

01:35:14.081 --> 01:35:15.684
He would've attacked
to Jujutsu High School

01:35:15.816 --> 01:35:17.284
whether you were here or not.

01:35:17.418 --> 01:35:18.553
You think so?

01:35:18.687 --> 01:35:20.454
I believe this is yours.

01:35:20.589 --> 01:35:22.022
Oh, my student ID.

01:35:22.156 --> 01:35:24.091
Thanks for finding
it for me, Gojo.

01:35:25.492 --> 01:35:28.762
No, it wasn't me.

01:35:28.896 --> 01:35:30.364
My best friend found it.

01:35:31.465 --> 01:35:33.200
My only friend really.

01:35:35.302 --> 01:35:36.270
Come on, Yuta.

01:35:36.403 --> 01:35:38.405
How long are you
gonna keep us waiting?

01:35:39.273 --> 01:35:40.274
Ready to go?

01:35:41.742 --> 01:35:44.579
(Yuta chuckles)

01:35:44.713 --> 01:35:47.414
(gentle music)

01:35:47.549 --> 01:35:48.749
[Yuta] Yeah.

01:35:59.728 --> 01:36:04.932
(singing in Japanese)

01:40:43.978 --> 01:40:49.182
(upbeat music)

01:41:08.168 --> 01:41:13.373
(singing in Japanese)

01:43:48.996 --> 01:43:51.933
(birds chirping)

01:43:58.338 --> 01:44:00.942
(horn honking)

01:44:02.043 --> 01:44:04.712
(car whooshing)

01:44:05.546 --> 01:44:08.716
(crowd chattering)

01:44:11.586 --> 01:44:14.387
(Yuta giggles)

01:44:16.356 --> 01:44:17.390
This is good.

01:44:17.525 --> 01:44:19.326
Didn't I tell you so?

01:44:19.459 --> 01:44:21.696
I used this great
spice called Royco.

01:44:21.829 --> 01:44:24.431
That's what gives it
that amazing flavor.

01:44:25.900 --> 01:44:27.168
Huh?

01:44:27.300 --> 01:44:29.070
Royco is a magic powder
that makes every dish taste

01:44:29.203 --> 01:44:31.973
like it was made in
Kenya when you add it in.

01:44:32.106 --> 01:44:35.610
More importantly, they really
went home, didn't they?

01:44:36.577 --> 01:44:37.879
(Yuta groans)

01:44:38.012 --> 01:44:38.913
For that I'm happy.

01:44:39.781 --> 01:44:41.182
[Yuta] This really is good.

01:44:41.314 --> 01:44:43.084
Reminds me of nikujaga.

01:44:43.217 --> 01:44:44.252
Nikujaga?

01:44:44.384 --> 01:44:45.520
That's too hard to pronounce,

01:44:45.653 --> 01:44:47.688
so let's just call
it, beef stew.

01:44:47.822 --> 01:44:49.724
(Miguel giggles)

01:44:49.857 --> 01:44:50.525
Hmm?

01:44:50.658 --> 01:44:51.926
What's the matter?

01:44:52.059 --> 01:44:55.462
[Miguel] Well, well,
what are you doing here?

01:44:56.764 --> 01:44:57.765
What the?

01:44:58.933 --> 01:44:59.600
Gojo?

01:44:59.734 --> 01:45:01.836
Hey, long time no see.
